{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '1,154p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t---\n     2\tdescription: Configurable and composable preludes for Yang language frontends — a three-tier hybrid architecture (pure host value core, unified guest %capture algebraic effects, minimal VM stream/cell effects) and portable semantics descriptors for native and Yin/Clojure frontend profiles.\n     3\t---\n     4\t\n     5\t# yang.preludes: configurable and composable preludes for Yang frontends\n     6\t\n     7\t**Status:** Proposed design, 2026-11-21 (r7 — Clojure-First Default & Legacy Track, plus DRY-alignment reconciliation). No implementation or completed acceptance gate is claimed.\n     8\t\n     9\t**Revision history:**\n    10\t- **2026-11-20 (r1 → r2 reconciliation):** Addressed all 10 findings (6 HIGH, 4 MEDIUM) from Lead System Architect review [`collab/yang-base/1795169993265-architect-yang-preludes-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md`](../../collab/yang-base/1795169993265-architect-yang-preludes-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md).\n    11\t- **2026-11-21 (r2 → r3 reconciliation):** Addressed all 8 remaining findings (`F1`–`F8`: 5 HIGH, 2 MEDIUM, 1 LOW) from Lead System Architect r2 review [`collab/yang-base/1795186644731-architect-yang-preludes-design-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md`](../../collab/yang-base/1795186644731-architect-yang-preludes-design-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md).\n    12\t- **2026-11-21 (r3 → r4 reconciliation):** Addressed all 13 remaining findings (9 HIGH, 3 MEDIUM, 1 LOW) from Lead System Architect r3 review [`collab/yang-base/1795196337796-architect-yang-preludes-design-r3.gpt-6.2-astra.findings.md`](../../collab/yang-base/1795196337796-architect-yang-preludes-design-r3.gpt-6.2-astra.findings.md).\n    13\t- **2026-11-21 (r4 → r5 reconciliation & clean-slate simplification):** Addressed all 9 remaining findings (7 HIGH, 1 MEDIUM, 1 LOW) from Jupiter Pool-2 r4 review [`collab/yang-base/1795198164100-architect-yang-preludes-design-r4-jupiter.gpt-6.2-astra.findings.md`](../../collab/yang-base/1795198164100-architect-yang-preludes-design-r4-jupiter.gpt-6.2-astra.findings.md) under the **Owner Clean-Slate Directive** (standardized prelude emitters uniformly and unified `clj` + `clojure.core` without a separate bridge or dual legacy Clojure stdlib).\n    14\t- **2026-11-21 (r5 → r6 hybrid architecture & focused profile scope):** Eliminated guest-UAST host-leak workarounds and collapsed fragmented control subsystems into a **three-tier hybrid model** (aligned with Unison, Koka, and OCaml 5): (1) promoted representation-sensitive pure ops (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `data/admit-key?`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed IEEE-754 `yin.vm.float`) into `:pure` host primitives backed by `dao.jing.cbor` / `dao.host.*`, eliminating raw-double stack-frame hazards and guest-side $O(n \\log n)$ sorting; (2) unified `yrt.escape`, `yrt.gen`, safepoint interrupt dispatch, and cold error/limit policy traps into one composable guest algebraic-effect layer (`yrt.effect`) over `%capture` with zero Jolt kernel expansion; (3) focused swappable preludes on **Native profiles** (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj` for existing code in those languages) plus **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profiles** (`yang.python/clojure-core-v1`, future `yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1`), dropping unnecessary off-diagonal N×M symmetry (such as `:yang.clojure/py-v1`).\n    15\t- **2026-11-21 (r6 → r7 Clojure-First Default & Legacy Track, plus landed-DRY reconciliation):** Three owner directives. **(D10) Default-profile inversion:** for `yang.python` (and later `yang.typescript`/`yang.php`), the **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profile is the DEFAULT** runtime profile; the native preludes (`py`/`js`/`php` semantics) become the **Legacy compatibility track** — kept frozen as landed (they already exist, oracle-parity-proven, at their current content addresses), with their *re-architecture* onto `yrt.*`/boxed float deferred until legacy demand justifies it. **(Clojure-first roadmap):** the implementation order re-sequenced so the Clojure prelude family (`yrt.effect`/`yrt.int` with Clojure-only consumers, unified trusted `clj`, `clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core` facade, `clj.py`, the python lowerer's descriptor parameterization) is built FIRST — the other-language native preludes are untouched by those slices (zero golden churn; defquoted consolidation and emitter standardization for py/ts/php defer to the legacy track). **(DRY-alignment reconciliation):** §5.2 admission checks home in `yang.core.prelude-admission` (3→5 publics, at bound) keeping `yang.core.prelude` pure emission; §8.2 names both the guest linker modules (`yrt.*`) and their host emitter namespaces (`src/cljc/yang/rt/*.cljc`) and acknowledges the analyzer's 3 self-loop warnings (macro self-reference, no multi-node cycles); defquoted consolidation accounted against the public-surface ledger; §2 gains the tao-architecture second-axiom alignment (the semantics descriptor is stream-resident interpreter configuration; the provenance tuple names the interpreter).\n    16\t\n    17\t**Authority:** Subordinate to [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md) (axioms, invariants, streams, host boundaries), [`adr/0004-external-effects-are-interpreted-stream-deposits.md`](./adr/0004-external-effects-are-interpreted-stream-deposits.md) (external effects as stream deposits), [`yang.antlr.md`](./yang.antlr.md) (§3 frontend SPI, §8.1–§8.2 semantic placement, §8.5.5 float addresses, §8.5.6 linked modules, §8.10 shared calling convention, §8.11 cells, §9 four-layer stdlib model), [`yang.typescript.md`](./yang.typescript.md) (§2.2 shared rulings, §17 lift enumeration, §19 owner decision A12.5), [`yang.php.md`](./yang.php.md) (§9 prelude inventory), [`yin.vm.linker.md`](./yin.vm.linker.md), [`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md), [`dao.jing.cbor.md`](./dao.jing.cbor.md), and [`src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md`](../../src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md).\n    18\t\n    19\t**Scope, Owner Clean-Slate Directive, and amendments:** This document settles owner decision A12.5 of `yang.typescript.md` §19 (the deferred `yrt` shared prelude lift) and extends `yang.antlr.md` §3.1/§3.4/§9.3 to treat preludes as **composable runtime modules** and **swappable frontend libraries** supporting both **native language profiles** (for existing Python, TypeScript, PHP, and Clojure programs) and **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profiles** (allowing familiar syntaxes such as `yang.python` or `yang.typescript` to compile directly onto `clojure.core` and persistent Yin data). Per the Owner Clean-Slate Directive (single-user system, zero legacy deployments), clean rewrites, uniform emitter normalization, direct `yang.clojure` migration onto `clojure.core`, and clean golden regeneration are explicitly preferred over maintaining dual legacy runtimes or frozen-quirk compatibility shims. It adds no UAST node type, no VM opcode, no manifest schema version, and no closed language registry.\n    20\t\n    21\t---\n    22\t\n    23\t## 1. Problem statement and repository baseline\n    24\t\n    25\t### 1.1 Current repository baseline\n    26\t\n    27\tTwo sharing mechanisms already exist in `src/cljc/yang/`:\n    28\t\n    29\t1. **Host-side emitter and admission machinery (`yang.core.*`):**\n    30\t   - `yang.core.prelude` (`src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc`): pure UAST builders and symbol strippers (`define`, `strip`, `module-definitions`, `wide-app`, `module-tree`, `exports`, `free-names`, `defined-keys`, `free-name-vec`, `definitions->uast`, `balanced-definitions->uast`).\n    31\t   - `yang.core.prelude-admission` (`src/cljc/yang/core/prelude_admission.cljc`): `host-declaration`, `module-spec`, and `admit` over `yin.vm` and `yin.vm.module`.\n    32\t   - `yang.core.module` and `yang.core.publication`: shared linker module naming, free-primitive declaration, SCC bundle/alias specs, and dependency-first publication.\n    33\t   - *(Residual host helper duplication:)* the ClojureDart AOT `defquoted` macro is still duplicated across `yang.python.antlr.prelude`, `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude`, and `yang.php.antlr.quoted`.\n    34\t2. **One shared guest runtime module (`yang.core.call`):**\n    35\t   - `src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc` emits the language-neutral calling convention (`yang.call`) using `yang.core.prelude` and `yang.core.prelude-admission`, with both a bundled tree (`uast`) and a linked module (`module-uast`, `module-spec`). All four frontends (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`) compose against it.\n    36\t\n    37\tDespite that shared plumbing, all remaining guest runtime code lives in four separate language preludes and three safepoint hook preludes:\n    38\t\n    39\t| Prelude namespace | Linker module | Size / definitions | Lowering coupling |\n    40\t|---|---|---|---|\n    41\t| `yang.python.antlr.prelude` | `py` | 4,188 LOC / 343 defs | `yang.python.antlr.lower` hardcodes 103 `py/*` names + `{:py/str}`, `{:py/float}`, `:py/None`, `:py/unbound` |\n    42\t| `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude` | `js` | 4,447 LOC / 475 defs | `yang.typescript.antlr.lower` hardcodes 93 `js/*` names + `:js/undefined`, `:js/null`, `:js/tdz`, `{:js/str}` |\n    43\t| `yang.php.antlr.prelude` (+ `_module`, `_p9`, `builtins`) | `php` | 8,150 LOC / 936 defs | `yang.php.antlr.lower` hardcodes 188 `php/*` names + `:php/null`, `{:php/type :array}`, etc. |\n    44\t| `yang.clojure.prelude` (+ inline family in `yang.clojure`) | `clj` | 250 LOC / 17 defs (+ `library`) | `yang.clojure` emits `clj/*` continuations and `yang.call/*` directly |\n    45\t| `yang.*.antlr.safepoint` | `pysp`, `jssp`, `php.sp` | 478 / 235 / 70 LOC | Hardcoded hook profiles |\n    46\t\n    47\t### 1.2 Three problems to solve together\n    48\t\n    49\t1. **Host representation leaks in guest UAST:** Bare VM primitives (`+`, `-`, `=`, `get`, `assoc`, `vec`, `kind/str`) delegate directly to host values, leaking JVM vs. Node/CLJS vs. Dart/CLJD vs. Jolt differences (`Float64` boxing, `BigInt` mixing, `NaN`/`-0.0` equality, CLJS joined-keyword collapse `(keyword nil \"a/b\") == (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`, HAMT map/set iteration order, float formatting). Patching around those leaks in guest UAST produces hundreds of lines of slow, fragile code (`admit-key!`, $O(n \\log n)$ `canonical-compare`, raw-double leaf-frame rules).\n    50\t2. **Duplicated, fragmented guest control mechanics:** ~1,200–2,000 lines of guest UAST across `py`, `js`, `php`, and `clj` duplicate `%capture` handler stacks, coroutine stepping (`gen-switch`), safepoint signal handling, and numeric error-status plumbing as four separate mechanisms instead of one composable guest algebraic-effect layer.\n    51\t3. **Hardcoded syntax-to-prelude coupling:** A frontend lowering currently assumes one fixed runtime profile. Even though `yang.frontend` (`src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc`) already tracks `:yang.frontend/grammar`, `:yang.frontend/lowering-profile`, `:yang.frontend/runtime-profile`, and `:yang.frontend/support-profile` independently, frontends cannot yet offer both their **native semantics profile** (for existing code in that language) and a **Yin/Clojure profile** (compiling Python or TypeScript syntax directly onto `clojure.core` and persistent Yin values).\n    52\t\n    53\t---\n    54\t\n    55\t## 2. Derivation from foundations and non-negotiable invariants\n    56\t\n    57\tThis design is constrained directly by `docs/design/datom.world.md`, `docs/design/adr/0004-external-effects-are-interpreted-stream-deposits.md`, and `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md`.\n    58\t\n    59\t### 2.1 Foundational axioms & three-tier hybrid rationale\n    60\t\n    61\t1. **Everything is a Stream:** Prelude selection, composition, and lowering are pure functions of explicit data configurations and CST streams. External I/O and host capabilities remain declared VM/stream effects (`stream/*`, `cell/*`, `:module/require`) per ADR 0004; prelude composition adds no ambient I/O.\n    62\t2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics:** A CST packet carries syntax only; its runtime meaning emerges from `(cst-packet, lowering-profile, semantics-descriptor, runtime-profile)`. Interpreting one Python CST under `:yang.python/py-v1` (CPython semantics) versus `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (Clojure persistent-data semantics) is a direct realization of \"one truth, many perspectives.\"\n    63\t3. **Code and State are Datoms (and Unitarity / Derive-Don't-Persist):**\n    64\t   - Lowering preserves source CST identity; compiled UAST roots under different preludes have distinct content addresses (or identical addresses when two descriptors emit identical UAST) linked by explicit provenance datoms pinning `(cst-address, lowering-profile, semantics-descriptor, runtime-profile, unit-address)`.\n    65\t   - Zero new AST tags, zero VM opcodes, and zero manifest schema changes are introduced. Linker manifests retain schema 1, and C1 `:yang/call-site` tables continue to publish beside manifests rather than inside them.\n    66\t   - Composition facts (which `yrt.*` modules a prelude requires) live in the explicit module `:requires` DAG, never as a redundant tag in UAST rows.\n    67\t4. **Everything is a Continuation (Hybrid Effect Boundary):**\n    68\t   Real-world algebraic-effect systems converge on one clean boundary: **Unison** keeps pure built-in value types (`Nat`/`Int`/`Float`/`Text`/`Bytes`) in the runtime, models control/errors/streams as pure user-handled abilities, and reserves only `IO` for the runtime; **Koka** keeps total math/data primitives effect-free (`total`) and draws the effect line at partiality (`exn`), divergence (`div`), state (`st`), and I/O; **OCaml 5** keeps hot synchronous ops native, reserves effect handlers for resumable control flow, and forbids effects from crossing raw native/C frames. Yin/Yang adopts the exact same three-tier split:\n    69\t   - **Pure host value core (`:pure` primitives):** Total, representation-sensitive math, equality, canonical ordering, key admission, and text ops stay native and fast across all 4 hosts.\n    70\t   - **Guest algebraic effects (`yrt.effect` over `%capture`):** Control flow (exceptions, `finally`, PHP `abandon-to`, resumable `yield`) and cold policy traps (`:math/div-zero`, `:math/overflow`, `:int/bit-limit`, `:int/digit-limit`, `:coll/unsupported-key`, `:runtime/interrupt`) live in pure guest UAST — zero Jolt kernel expansion.\n    71\t   - **VM / stream effects (`make-effect` → `:effect-handlers`):** Strictly `cell/*`, `stream/*`, `:module/require`, and bound external surfaces per ADR 0004.\n    72\t\n    73\t### 2.1a Alignment with the tao architecture's second axiom (`yang.tao.md` §2.2)\n    74\t\n    75\tThe semantics descriptor and profile pinning are a direct application of the governing axiom **Everything is a Stream** and its invariant *Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream*:\n    76\t\n    77\t- **Interpreter configuration is stream-resident data.** `yang.tao.md` §2.2 requires that \"the grammar, name environment, and elaborator configuration participate in interpretation\" and that \"an interpretation result must name both its input and the interpreter that produced it.\" The hardcoded `py/*`-style coupling in the current lowerers buried that configuration in host code; the `:yang.semantics/descriptor` and `:yang.prelude/profile` lift it into portable, content-addressed artifacts, and the provenance tuple `(cst-address, lowering-profile, semantics-descriptor, runtime-profile, unit-address)` names the interpreter exactly.\n    78\t- **\"One truth, many perspectives\" is a stream operation.** The same Python CST packet is one truth; `py-v1` and `clojure-core-v1` are two perspectives. Selecting between them — the wolf-in-sheep's-clothing inversion — is a *re-pin of stream-resident artifacts* (the descriptor and profile addresses), never a callback into the lowerer and never ambient prelude state.\n    79\t- **The \"explicit local functions\" clause is where the ambient resolver lives:** the `:kind :cell-accessor` projections resolve through the unit-bound `ambient-resolver` passed as data (`[body-fn ambient-resolver]`) — a task-local cell of cells, explicit, named in the provenance, and validated against verified UAST before use.\n    80\t\n    81\tConsequence: switching a frontend's default semantics is a *data re-pin* (revision selection in `yang.frontend`), carrying zero code change and zero content-address churn for unselected profiles.\n    82\t\n    83\t### 2.2 Non-negotiable invariants\n    84\t\n    85\t1. **No hidden global state — stateless `yrt.*` modules:**\n    86\t   - `yang.core.*` holds no mutable global registry of preludes or languages (`yang.frontend` immutable catalog rule).\n    87\t   - **Shared `yrt.*` modules own zero `*.rt/*` state cells.** Every stateful `yrt.*` function takes the caller's task-local state cell (e.g., `ctx-cell`) as an explicit parameter. When a single Yin task links independent foreign language runtimes (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`) together via `yang.call`, each foreign runtime maintains its own isolated handler stack and depth/base accounting inside its own `*.rt/ctx` cell rather than aliasing or corrupting another language's stack.\n    88\t   - **Intentional intra-Clojure domain sharing:** By explicit architectural design, `clj`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, and `clojure.core` execute *inside* the Clojure semantics and exception domain and therefore share `(clj/rt-ctx)` intentionally so Clojure `(throw ...)` / `(try ... (finally ...))` and Python-syntax `try` / `except` / `finally` unwind across `clj → clj.py → clj` nesting on one coherent handler stack while saving and restoring `(clj/rt-ctx)` at every `yrt.effect/try-value` and `finally` boundary.\n    89\t2. **No implicit control flow:** All escapes and resumptions remain explicit continuation invocations over an explicit handler chain.\n    90\t3. **No raw callbacks & no raw host doubles in guest frames:** Policy handlers and closures passed into `yrt.*` are ordinary guest Yin closures, never host-boundary callbacks. By boxing IEEE-754 float operations at the `yin.vm.float` host boundary, unwrapped host doubles never appear on guest stacks, making `%capture` and safepoints safe everywhere.\n    91\t4. **No shared mutable state:** Each stateful profile allocates its own task-local cells once per task in its own idempotent `init!` under its own private namespace (`py.rt/*`, `js.rt/*`, `php.rt/*`, `clj.rt/*`, `clj.py.rt/*`, `clojure.core.rt/*`); `clojure.core.impl` is pure and stateless.\n    92\t5. **No layer collapsing:** Parsing (host ANTLR boundary) → lowering (syntax + frontend lowering contract + semantics descriptor → UAST) → prelude composition & admission (pure spec/artifact verification; never publishes or executes) → publication/linking → VM execution stay separated across explicit stream/module boundaries.\n    93\t6. **No assumed graphs:** Every composed prelude declares an explicit, acyclic `:requires` DAG over an **immutable, verified artifact closure**. Missing exports, missing transitive artifacts, or cycles fail closed at validation/admission time before publication or execution.\n    94\t7. **No closed language registry (`yang.antlr.md` owner directive):** Neither `yrt.*` nor `yang.core.*` contains a `case`/dispatch over `:python`, `:typescript`, `:php`, or `:clojure`, inspects `:py/type`/`:js/type`/`:php/type`/`:clj/type` tags, or encodes language-specific lowering ABI tables.\n    95\t8. **Security boundary — VM provenance doors stay private:** Under `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md` and `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc`, `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance` are reserved compiler/runtime-module doors whose names guest code must not forge or re-export.\n    96\t   - **`yrt.*` modules, `clj.py`, and Layer-2c standard libraries (`clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) MUST NEVER declare (`:yin.module/primitives`) or export (`:yin.module/exports`) provenance-door primitives directly.** (Transitive `:yin.module/footprint` unions are governed by `:yang.prelude/max-effects`.)\n    97\t   - **No descriptor hook or source-facing ambient projection** may expose `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or non-projectable internal implementation modules such as `*.impl/*` (`clojure.core.impl/*`) (`§6.3`).\n    98\t   - Retained protocol-condition provenance (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10.7) resides strictly inside trusted Layer-2b runtime modules (`py`, `js`, `php`, **`clj`**) in **both** bundled (`uast`) and linked (`module-uast`) emission, never exported and never exposed across `yrt.*`, Layer-2c libraries, or source scope.\n    99\t\n   100\t---\n   101\t\n   102\t## 3. Three-tier hybrid architecture & prelude layering\n   103\t\n   104\t`yang.antlr.md` §9.1 Layer 2 (\"Language intrinsics and preludes\") sits directly on top of a small, portable `:pure` host value core and minimal VM effect boundary:\n   105\t\n   106\t```text\n   107\t+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   108\t| Layer 2c: Ambient & Standard Libraries (clojure.core, clojure.core.impl, …) |\n   109\t|   Ordinary compiled linker modules; explicit projections enter source scope |\n   110\t+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   111\t                                      ^\n   112\t                                      | binds / lowers through\n   113\t+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   114\t| Layer 2b: Semantics-Protocol Libraries (py, js, php, clj, clj.py)           |\n   115\t|   Language value encodings, coercions, effect handlers, state cells, init!  |\n   116\t+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   117\t                                      ^\n   118\t                                      | composes explicitly via :requires DAG\n   119\t+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   120\t| Layer 2a: Composable Guest Building Blocks (yang.call, yrt.effect, yrt.int, |\n   121\t|   yrt.safepoint) — stateless guest UAST over %capture + :pure host core     |\n   122\t+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   123\t                                      ^\n   124\t              +-----------------------+-----------------------+\n   125\t              |                                               |\n   126\t+-------------+-------------------------+     +---------------+---------------+\n   127\t| Tier 1: Native Host :pure Core        |     | Tier 3: Minimal VM Effects    |\n   128\t|   data | integer | float | kind       |     |   cell | stream | :module/req |\n   129\t|   (universal truth, zero suspension)  |     |   (state & ADR-0004 I/O ABI)  |\n   130\t+---------------------------------------+     +-------------------------------+\n   131\t```\n   132\t\n   133\t### 3.1 Litmus test: Native Host `:pure` vs. Guest `%capture` Effects vs. VM Effects\n   134\t\n   135\t| Tier | Mechanism | Inclusion criteria | Examples |\n   136\t|---|---|---|---|\n   137\t| **Tier 1: Native Host `:pure` Core** | Host module exports (`:pure`, effects `#{}`) in `data`, `integer`, `float`, `kind` | **All four hold:** (1) one universal mathematical/representational truth across all languages and all 4 hosts; (2) host-representation-sensitive (avoids `Float64`/`BigInt`/keyword/HAMT leaks); (3) total or status-returning without suspending control flow or calling guest closures; (4) hot-path value operation. | Exact big-int math, boxed IEEE-754 float math & formatting, `data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `data/admit-key?`, `kind/namespace`, code-point strings. |\n   138\t| **Tier 2: Guest Algebraic Effects** | `yrt.effect` over `%capture` + task-local handler stack (100% guest UAST) | **Any holds:** (1) language-specific or swappable policy (`OverflowError` vs. `Infinity` vs. PHP int64 demotion, test replay); (2) non-local control flow (exceptions, `finally`, PHP `abandon-to`, resumable `yield`); (3) cold/error path; (4) must invoke guest closures. **Zero Jolt kernel cost.** | `raise`/`try`/`finally`, `call-ec`, `abandon-to`, resumable `yield` generators, cold traps (`:math/div-zero`, `:math/overflow`, `:int/bit-limit`, `:int/digit-limit`, `:coll/unsupported-key`), `:runtime/interrupt`. |\n   139\t| **Tier 3: VM / Stream Effects** | `make-effect` → VM `:effect-handlers` | State, module loading, and external world capabilities only (ADR 0004). Never language-specific semantics. | `cell/*`, `stream/*` (`stream/poll!` safepoints), `:module/require`, bound external I/O surfaces. |\n   140\t\n   141\t### 3.2 Explicit exclusions from Layer 2a (`yrt.*`)\n   142\t\n   143\tThe following remain in Layer 2b (per-language preludes) because unifying them either breaks semantic fidelity or forces a closed type-tag dispatch:\n   144\t\n   145\t| Mechanism | Why it stays in Layer 2b |\n   146\t|---|---|\n   147\t| **Ordered maps / dicts / arrays** | Python dicts normalize `1 == 1.0 == True` via exact rationals and tuple-key recursion; JS own-key maps sort uint32 indices ahead of strings and symbols; PHP arrays coerce int64-looking strings, track `:next-index`, and implement copy-on-write refcounted handles. |\n   148\t| **Module / import loaders** | Python `sys.modules` + package hierarchy, JS ESM link/eval stacks + live bindings, and PHP dynamic `include`/`require` scope-cell adoption have incompatible lifecycle rules. |\n   149\t| **Object / class / prototype dispatch** | MRO/descriptors (`py`), prototype chains/accessors (`js`), and traits/refcounted destructors (`php`) belong to `yang.antlr.md` §9.4 Layer 3. |\n   150\t| **Provenance doors** | `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance` are security-sensitive VM doors (`§2.2` invariant 8). |\n   151\t| **PHP `php.sp` budget/ticks hooks** | `php.sp` uses a decrementing execution-budget cell (`php.sp/remaining`) and `:line :after` statement ticks rather than `stream/poll!` signal cursors. |\n   152\t\n   153\t---\n   154\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '155,332p'\"","aggregated_output":"   155\t## 4. Host `:pure` core extensions & Layer 2a (`yrt.*`) specifications\n   156\t\n   157\t### 4.1 Native host `:pure` core extensions (`data`, `float`, `kind`)\n   158\t\n   159\tExisting `yin.vm.integer` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc`, v4) and `yin.vm.data` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc`) already establish the `:pure` host-module pattern: total or keyword-status-returning kernels over `dao.host.*` and `dao.jing.cbor` with zero guest callbacks and identical semantics across JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, and Jolt/Scheme.\n   160\t\n   161\tTo eliminate host representation leaks and raw-double stack-frame hazards across all frontends, we add a small, cohesive set of `:pure` exports (zero changes to VM opcodes or `yin.vm/primitives`):\n   162\t\n   163\t1. **Additions to `yin.vm.data` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc`):**\n   164\t   - **`data/float64? [x]`:** Backed directly by existing `dao.jing.cbor/float64?` (`src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:212`). Distinguishes float64 carriers from exact integers, booleans, and maps on all 4 hosts.\n   165\t   - **`data/equiv [a b]`:** Portable IEEE-aware, kind-strict value equality (distinct from content-addressing `data/content=`):\n   166\t     - Exact int × exact int: `integer/compare == 0`; float64 × float64: `false` if either is `NaN`, else IEEE numeric equality (`+0.0 == -0.0` is `true`, `NaN == NaN` is `false`); exact int × float64: **`false`** (`1 != 1.0`).\n   167\t     - Keywords/symbols: strict kind + nullable namespace + name equality, so `(keyword nil \"a/b\") == (keyword \"a\" \"b\")` is **`false`** on CLJS/Node as well as JVM/Dart/Jolt.\n   168\t     - Persistent vectors/lists, maps (excluding `:cell-ref` handles), and sets: recursive pairwise/entry equality using `data/equiv`.\n   169\t     - Other scalars (`nil`, booleans, strings, authenticated `:cell-ref` handles): host `=`.\n   170\t   - **`data/admit-key? [k]`:** Recursive portable key/element predicate preventing host map/set collapse (`yin/vm/data.cljc:34–36`, `dao.jing.cbor.md:173, 266`). Returns `true` iff `k` (recursively across vectors, maps, and sets) contains only `nil`, booleans, exact integers, strings, and unambiguous keywords/symbols (`ns` non-empty and free of `\"/\"`, `name` free of `\"/\"` and not starting with `\":\"`); returns `false` for any `float64?` (at any nesting depth), ambiguous identifiers, seqs/lists, closures/continuations, or `:cell-ref` handles.\n   171\t   - **`data/canonical-compare [a b]`:** Total, deterministic comparator over admitted keys/elements matching Jing's canonical order across all 4 hosts (type ranks: `nil < bool < exact-int < string < keyword(ns, name) < symbol(ns, name) < vector < map < set`, with recursive lexicographic comparison for compound values).\n   172\t   - **`data/canonical-entries [coll]`:** For a map, returns a vector of `[k v]` pairs sorted ascending by `data/canonical-compare` on `k`; for a set, returns a vector of elements sorted ascending by `data/canonical-compare`. Eliminates guest-UAST $O(n \\log n)$ sorting for `keys`, `vals`, `seq`, `reduce`, and `str`.\n   173\t2. **Boxed IEEE-754 host module `yin.vm.float` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/float.cljc`, module name `'float`):**\n   174\t   - Operates exclusively on **boxed `data/float64`** inputs and outputs (plus exact integers where specified), returning either a boxed `data/float64`, a boolean/integer/string, or a pure status keyword (`:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, `:yin.vm.float/underflow`, `:yin.vm.float/out-of-range`, `:yin.vm.float/fractional-exp`, `:yin.vm.float/infinite-exp`).\n   175\t   - **Zero raw host doubles in guest UAST:** Because guest code never unwraps a host double across stack frames, `%capture` effects and safepoints can never observe an unwrapped host double — retiring the fragile raw-double leaf-frame rules of r1–r5 completely.\n   176\t   - **Exports (all `:pure`, effects `#{}`):**\n   177\t     - Constants/predicates: `inf`, `neg-inf`, `nan`, `zero`, `neg-zero`, `nan?`, `finite?`, `zero?`, `neg-zero?`, `zero-like`.\n   178\t     - Core IEEE arithmetic: `add`, `sub`, `mul`, `div` (returns boxed IEEE result, or `:yin.vm.float/div-zero` on `div-checked` when `y == 0.0`), `neg` (preserves `-0.0 ↔ +0.0`), `abs`, `compare` (`-1`/`0`/`1` or `:yin.vm.float/nan`).\n   179\t     - Division/floor/power: `floor` (total IEEE double floor), `floor-int` (exact integer for finite `|x| < 2^53`, else `:yin.vm.float/out-of-range`), `fmod-pos` (Sterbenz remainder for finite `x >= 0, y > 0`), `floordiv-mod` (returns `[q r]` boxed pair or `:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, preserving `-0.0` quotient sign and `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0` rounding correction), `fpow-half` (half-power squaring for `py`/`js`/`clj.py`), `fpow-base` (base squaring for `php`, preserving `1.1 ** 6` bit-exact oracle parity — see D7), `neg-pow` (`[x n pow-order]`, returns boxed `float64` or `:yin.vm.float/underflow`), `parts` (`[mantissa exp2]` exact integer pair).\n   180\t     - Formatting: `format` (deterministic 4-host decimal/scientific formatting over `dao.host.float/float-digits`, rendering `NaN`, `Infinity`, `-Infinity`, `0.0`, `-0.0`, `1.0 -> \"1.0\"` identically on JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt).\n   181\t3. **Addition to `yang.clojure/kind-module`:**\n   182\t   - **`kind/namespace [x]`:** One `:pure` unary export backed by `namespace`, enabling deterministic symbol/keyword rendering in `clojure.core.impl`.\n   183\t\n   184\t### 4.2 `yang.call` *(existing Layer-2a leaf)*\n   185\t\n   186\tRemains unchanged at `src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc` (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10): structural callable discovery (`entry`, `eligible?`), invocation records (`invocation`, `invocation-with`, `valid-invocation?`), and condition transfer (`condition`, `thrown`, `transfer`, `invoke`, `invoke-with`). Requires no `yrt.*` module so `yang.call` stays a leaf dependency.\n   187\t\n   188\t### 4.3 `yrt.effect` — Unified guest algebraic effects over `%capture`\n   189\t\n   190\tUsed by: `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`, `clj.py`, `yrt.int`, `yrt.safepoint`. Host dependencies: `cell/get`, `cell/set!`, `cell/new`, `data/nth`.\n   191\t\n   192\tEvery Layer-2a module follows `yang.core.call`'s single-source dual-emitter pattern: one ordered definition vector emitting both a bundled `uast` (tail-marked) and a linked `module-uast` + `module-spec` (wide-app over stripped definitions, C1-finalized call sites, and `prelude-admission/module-spec`).\n   193\t\n   194\t`yrt.effect` replaces separate `yrt.escape`, `yrt.gen`, and ad-hoc error-callback plumbing with **one composable guest algebraic-effect handler model** over `%capture` and an explicit task-local `ctx-cell`:\n   195\t\n   196\t- **Unified context record:** `{:handlers hs :depth d :base b :frame f}`.\n   197\t  - **4-to-5-slot migration for `js` and `clj`:** In P1, `js/init!`, `clj/init!`, and bundled `yang.clojure` migrate from 4-slot frames to `(yrt.effect/ctx nil 0 0 nil)` and 5-slot frames `[kind payload rest n depth]`:\n   198\t    - `kind`: `:finally` (cleanup frame), `:handler` (abortive exception handler), `:effect` (tagged resumable/abortive effect handler), or any language-installed boundary tag (such as `:generator` during P1→P4 migration).\n   199\t    - `payload`: cleanup closure `fin` (for `:finally`), abortive continuation `r` (for `:handler`), or `[tag handler-fn outer-k]` (for `:effect`).\n   200\t    - `rest`: enclosing frame (or `nil`).\n   201\t    - **`n` (slot 3):** monotonic handler-stack frame count `(+ 1 (frame-depth rest))` for $O(1)$ structural depth comparison (`<= (data/nth hs 3) n`).\n   202\t    - **`depth` (slot 4):** activation-relative call depth restored onto `:depth` by `pop-frame` (`py`/`php` recursion accounting; `0` for `js`/`clj`).\n   203\t- **Capture-safe vector frame reads (`data/nth`):** Every read of the 5-slot frame vector uses **`data/nth`**, reserving `get` strictly for context-map fields (`:handlers`, `:depth`, `:base`). Source-defined `(defn get ...)` can never corrupt frame dispatch.\n   204\t- **`restore!` invariant:** `(fn [ctx-cell saved] (cell/set! ctx-cell (assoc saved :base (get (cell/get ctx-cell) :base))))` — preserves live `:base` across generator/coroutine crossings.\n   205\t\n   206\t**Public exports:**\n   207\t\n   208\t| Category | Export | Signature | Behavior |\n   209\t|---|---|---|---|\n   210\t| **Context & frames** | `ctx`, `handlers`, `set-handlers!`, `restore!`, `frame-depth`, `frame`, `pop-frame` | `[...]` | Stateless context-cell accessors and 5-slot frame constructors (`restore!` preserves live `:base`). |\n   211\t| **Abortive control (exceptions & escapes)** | `raise` | `[ctx-cell e on-empty]` | Unwind `:finally` frames passing `e`; deliver `e` to the first enclosing `:handler` (or non-`:finally` boundary frame); call `(on-empty e)` if empty. |\n   212\t| | `try-value` / `try-orelse` | `[ctx-cell body handler]` / `[ctx-cell body handler orelse]` | Install `:handler`; on normal exit restore and return `(body)` (or tail-call `(orelse)` for `py`/`php`/`clj.py`); on escape restore and call `(handler e)`. |\n   213\t| | `try-finally` | `[ctx-cell body fin normal-arg]` | Install `:finally`; on normal exit restore, run `(fin normal-arg)`, return `v`. |\n   214\t| | `unwind-to` / `call-ec` | `[ctx-cell n normal-arg]` / `[ctx-cell f normal-arg]` | Pop frames down to depth `n` running `:finally` thunks with `normal-arg` (`:py/None`, `:js/undefined`, `:php/null`, `nil`), then restore and jump. |\n   215\t| | `abandon-to` / `call-terminal` | `[ctx-cell n]` / `[ctx-cell f]` | Pop frames down to depth `n` **without** running `:finally` thunks (PHP fatal exit). |\n   216\t| **Resumable & tagged algebraic effects** | `handle` | `[ctx-cell tag handler-fn body]` | Install an `:effect` frame for `tag` around `(body)`. When `(perform ctx-cell tag payload)` fires inside `body`, `yrt.effect` captures the delimited continuation `k`, restores the outer context, and invokes `(handler-fn payload k)` — where `handler-fn` may either abort (returning a value or calling `raise`) or resume `(k v)` one-shot with a computed value. |\n   217\t| | `perform` | `[ctx-cell tag payload on-unhandled]` | Captures the current continuation via `%capture`, walks `ctx-cell` to the nearest matching `:effect` frame for `tag` (without running `:finally` frames unless the handler aborts without resuming), and invokes `(handler-fn payload k)`. If no matching handler exists, calls `(on-unhandled tag payload)`. |\n   218\t\n   219\t- **One mechanism for four subsystems:**\n   220\t  1. **Exceptions & escapes:** `try-value`, `try-orelse`, `try-finally`, `call-ec`, `call-terminal` (abortive fast path).\n   221\t  2. **Cold numeric/resource policy traps:** Pure host ops (`yin.vm.integer`, `yin.vm.float`, `data/admit-key?`) return values on the hot path and status keywords on the cold path. Thin guest wrappers call `(yrt.effect/perform ctx :math/overflow ...)` / `:math/div-zero` / `:int/bit-limit` / `:int/digit-limit` / `:coll/unsupported-key` only on the cold branch — letting each language install its own policy handler (e.g., Python `OverflowError`/`MemoryError`/`ZeroDivisionError`, JS `Infinity`/`NaN`, PHP int64-to-float demotion, or deterministic test replay).\n   222\t  3. **Generators / coroutines (Track B — deferred):** `yield` is simply `(yrt.effect/perform ctx :gen/yield value)` handled by a coroutine driver that stores the captured continuation `k` and resumes `(k sent-val)` on `.next()`/`.send()`, with explicit `on-start-ctx` / `on-resume-ctx` hooks preserving Python `:base` rebasing vs. PHP direct context restoration and refcount cleanup.\n   223\t  4. **Safepoint interrupts (Track B — deferred):** `yrt.safepoint` polls `stream/poll!` (VM effect) and performs `:runtime/interrupt` via `yrt.effect` when a signal arrives (Python maps to `KeyboardInterrupt` / registered signal handler; JS maps to uncatchable root unwind).\n   224\t\n   225\t**Capture-safety for bundled `yang.clojure`:**\n   226\t- When `yrt.effect/uast` is bundled inline into non-linked `yang.clojure`, `[get = assoc]` bind to portable guest closures `[dsg__get dsg__equal dsg__assoc]` (with `dsg__get` supporting both maps and vectors via `data/nth`), `conj` relies on binder-check refusal, and `+`/`<=` use portable guest closures `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte`. In linked mode, module lexical isolation makes `dsg__*` unnecessary.\n   227\t\n   228\t### 4.4 `yrt.int` — Exact-integer adapters and radix scanners\n   229\t\n   230\tUsed by: `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj.py` (omitted by `clj`). Host dependencies: `data/count`, `data/nth`, `integer/*`. Requires: `yrt.effect`.\n   231\t\n   232\t- **`yin.vm.integer` v4 refusal algebra (`src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:81–100`):** Returns keyword reasons for `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit`, `:yin.vm.integer/digit-limit`, and `:yin.vm.integer/float-overflow`; every other refusal (`:arity`, `:wrong-type`, `:out-of-range`, `:syntax`, `:zero-division`, `:negative-count`, `:negative-exponent`) throws a host operational failure and **MUST NOT** be caught or relabeled into guest exceptions.\n   233\t- **Public exports:**\n   234\t  - `check-limit [ctx-cell res]` (and direct callback variant `check-limit-with [res on-bit on-digit on-float]`): returns `res` untouched on the hot path; on any of the three limit keywords, performs `:int/bit-limit`, `:int/digit-limit`, or `:math/overflow` via `yrt.effect/perform` (or invokes the supplied policy closure).\n   235\t  - Fixed-width wrapping: `wrap-unsigned [x width-pow2 mask]`, `wrap-signed [x half-range range]`, `in-range? [x min-v max-v]` (backing `js/wrap32` and `php/wrap64` / `php/int-result`).\n   236\t  - Generic radix digit scanners: `digit-value [cp]`, `all-digits? [cs i n radix]`, `scan-digits [cs i n radix acc]`, `skip-while [cs i n pred?]`, `skip-zeros [cs i n]`.\n   237\t  - Per-language integer floors (`min-integer-bits = 53` for `py`/`js`/`clj.py`; `min-integer-bits = 4096, min-integer-digits = 1000` for `php`) remain enforced by each profile's admission check.\n   238\t\n   239\t### 4.5 `yrt.safepoint` *(Track B — deferred)*\n   240\t\n   241\tExtracts `stream/cursor`, `stream/poll!` gap/signal detection, and `attach!` setup into one shared module (`yrt.safepoint`, requiring `yrt.effect` and host `stream`). When `stream/poll!` returns a signal, `yrt.safepoint` performs `:runtime/interrupt` via `yrt.effect/perform`, keeping signal delivery policy (`KeyboardInterrupt` in `pysp`; uncatchable root `Interrupt` unwind in `jssp`) and recursion depth counting (`pysp`) in each hook module.\n   242\t\n   243\t---\n   244\t\n   245\t## 5. Declarative prelude composition, recipes, and admission\n   246\t\n   247\tTo eliminate ad-hoc `module-spec` and `admit` boilerplate while keeping every runtime dependency completely reproducible and content-pinned, **build-time emission recipes** and **immutable deployment profiles** are separated cleanly.\n   248\t\n   249\t### 5.1 Emission recipe vs. resolved runtime profile\n   250\t\n   251\t1. **`:yang.prelude/recipe` (host-side compiler recipe that *emits* a runtime module):**\n   252\t   ```clojure\n   253\t   {:yang.prelude/schema 1\n   254\t    :yang.prelude/id :yang.python/py-prelude\n   255\t    :yang.prelude/revision \"2026-11-21.1\"\n   256\t    :yang.prelude/module 'py\n   257\t    :yang.prelude/components\n   258\t    [[yang.call \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   259\t     [yrt.effect \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   260\t     [yrt.int \"<blake3-address>\"]]\n   261\t    :yang.prelude/host-modules\n   262\t    {:cell {:required true}\n   263\t     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n   264\t     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}\n   265\t     :float {:required true}}\n   266\t    :yang.prelude/emitter\n   267\t    {:mode :linear                 ;; :linear (definitions->uast) | :balanced (balanced-definitions->uast)\n   268\t     :uninit :py/uninit\n   269\t     :rt-namespaces #{\"py.rt\" \"py.b\"}\n   270\t     :unshadow-locals? false\n   271\t     :trailing-requires []         ;; `[]` for base preludes (`py`/`js`/`php`/`clj`/`yang.call`), `['py]`/`['js]` only for safepoint overlays\n   272\t     :finalize-c1? true            ;; annotate `:yang/call-site 1` uniformly across all emitted preludes\n   273\t     :capture-safe-primitives nil} ;; optional for bundled clj mode\n   274\t    :yang.prelude/max-effects nil  ;; optional effect-ceiling set; nil = derive without extra ceiling\n   275\t    :yang.prelude/refusal-ns \"yang.python.antlr\"}\n   276\t   ```\n   277\t2. **`:yang.prelude/profile` (immutable, content-addressed runtime profile after publication):**\n   278\t   Replaces local build knobs with `:yang.prelude/root-address` (the published content address of the owning runtime module) alongside the pinned transitive closure:\n   279\t   ```clojure\n   280\t   {:yang.prelude/schema 1\n   281\t    :yang.prelude/id :yang.python/py-prelude\n   282\t    :yang.prelude/revision \"2026-11-21.1\"\n   283\t    :yang.prelude/module 'py\n   284\t    :yang.prelude/root-address \"<blake3-address-of-published-py-module>\"\n   285\t    :yang.prelude/components\n   286\t    [[yang.call \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   287\t     [yrt.effect \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   288\t     [yrt.int \"<blake3-address>\"]]\n   289\t    :yang.prelude/host-modules\n   290\t    {:cell {:required true}\n   291\t     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n   292\t     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}\n   293\t     :float {:required true}}\n   294\t    :yang.prelude/max-effects nil}\n   295\t   ```\n   296\t   A `:yang.prelude/profile` contains zero host functions or closures and passes `yang.frontend/non-portable-path`.\n   297\t\n   298\t### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n   299\t\n   300\t`yang.core.prelude` and `yang.core.prelude-admission` enforce six fail-closed checks. **Home rule (DRY-alignment, r7):** the composition checks (`validate-profile`, `admit-profile`, and their six sub-checks) are implemented in **`yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3 → 5 publics, exactly at the bounded-complexity target), keeping `yang.core.prelude` pure UAST/s-expression emission — the emission/admission boundary is the landed batch-1 seam (`1604aabe`), and the C2 lesson (module duplicating prelude's `host-declaration` was the duplication removed) requires one admission authority, not two namespaces sharing the checks:\n   301\t\n   302\t1. **Verified artifact closure input (`validate-profile`):** Takes `(profile artifact-store registry)`, where `artifact-store` supplies an immutable content-addressed map of published manifests (`manifest-addr -> verified-manifest`) AND their referenced canonical module trees (`tree-addr -> verified-uast`). Verifies that direct root pins match `:yang.prelude/components`, walks the full transitive `:requires` DAG from `:yang.prelude/root-address`, confirms finiteness and acyclicity, and refuses duplicate bindings for the same linker module symbol.\n   303\t2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):** Distinct Layer-2a/2b/2c modules may share bare local export names across qualified module borders; collisions are refused on duplicate linker module symbols, duplicate stripped local `module-definitions` keys, or duplicate source-facing `:ambient-projections` aliases (`§6.3`).\n   304\t3. **Provenance-door security exclusion (direct declarations, not transitive footprint):** Checks each non-trusted module's (`yrt.*`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) **direct** `:yin.module/primitives` (refusing `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance`) and **direct** `:yin.module/exports` (refusing any `dsg__*` export on **every** module including trusted Layer-2b runtimes), while governing transitive `:yin.module/footprint` through `:yang.prelude/max-effects`.\n   305\t4. **Effect-ceiling verification (`:yang.prelude/max-effects`):** Optional ceiling checked via `(clojure.set/subset? derived-transitive-effects max-effects)` over the verified `:yin.module/footprint :effects` union.\n   306\t5. **Host-module and limit admission (`admit-profile`):** Takes `(profile artifact-store registry host-limits)`, verifies every required host export (`prelude-admission/admit`), and enforces declared numeric floors (`:min-bits`, `:min-digits`, `:min-max-items`) against `host-limits` (failing closed if absent or below floor).\n   307\t6. **Dual-emitter standardization & Parity Law:** Standardized linked emission (`P0`) sets `:trailing-requires []` for base preludes (`['py]`/`['js]` only for safepoint overlays) and `:finalize-c1? true` uniformly. Any program compiled under a composed prelude MUST produce identical outcomes in bundled and linked modes across the semantic, stack, and register VMs (and the AST walker once L-b lands).\n   308\t\n   309\t---\n   310\t\n   311\t## 6. Preludes as swappable libraries: the semantics descriptor contract\n   312\t\n   313\t### 6.1 Focused profile scope: Yin/Clojure DEFAULT + Native legacy track\n   314\t\n   315\tSwappable preludes serve two concrete, complementary goals. **Per owner directive D10 (r7), the Yin/Clojure profiles are the DEFAULT runtime profiles** for the parameterized frontends; the native profiles become the Legacy compatibility track, kept frozen as landed and re-architected later only on demand:\n   316\t\n   317\t1. **Yin/Clojure profiles (`N → 1` — the DEFAULT, e.g. `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`):** New `datom.world` code, scripts, and agents are written in familiar Python or TypeScript syntax compiled directly onto `clojure.core`, persistent Yin collections, and `dao.stream` effects — with zero mutable-object baggage or marshalling overhead. The wolf in sheep's clothing: the syntax is the familiar grammar; the semantics are Clojure's persistent, immutable, functional core. Per the truth-in-advertising invariant (§7.1) the descriptor *declares* this — capability refusals fail closed, and equality/truthiness differences are contract, not accident.\n   318\t2. **Native language profiles (`py`, `js`, `php` — the Legacy compatibility track, built later):** Preserve full, faithful CPython/Node/PHP semantics for existing libraries and code that assumes them. The landed preludes already provide this at their current content addresses and remain the regression net (their oracle suites keep passing untouched). What defers is their *re-architecture* onto `yrt.*`/boxed float — a separate legacy-modernization track, undertaken only when legacy demand justifies it. Until then they run exactly as landed: frozen mechanisms, zero golden churn, selectable by pinning their revision.\n   319\t\n   320\t**Explicit non-goal (avoiding unnecessary N×M complexity):** We do **not** require arbitrary off-diagonal swaps (such as compiling `yang.clojure` syntax onto Python mutable dicts or PHP syntax onto JS prototypes). `yang.clojure` compiles directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core` without being forced through a generic hook ABI. Non-Clojure frontends (`yang.python`, `yang.typescript`, `yang.php`) parameterize their lowering through `:yang.semantics/descriptor` to select between their native profile and a Yin/Clojure profile (or custom ambient library projections).\n   321\t\n   322\t### 6.2 Core vs. Frontend ownership boundary\n   323\t\n   324\tTo preserve `yang.antlr.md` §3 (\"Yang core contains no enumeration of supported languages\"):\n   325\t- **`yang.core.semantics` (language-agnostic)** owns ONLY:\n   326\t  1. Generic schema validation for `:yang.semantics/descriptor`.\n   327\t  2. Pure, closed literal-strategy emission (`:raw`, `:float64-raw`, `:tagged-map`, `:raw-or-call`).\n   328\t  3. Generic capability lookup, hook-hygiene validation (every hook must be namespace-qualified), UAST-derived structural export/arity/role verification against the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure** across **every** executable descriptor field (hooks, executable literal strategies such as `:literals.*.overflow-op`, and ambient projections), and reserved-door projection checks.\n   329\t- **Each parameterized frontend package (e.g. `yang.python.antlr.contract`)** owns:\n   330\t  1. Its **fixed Hook ABI table** (`{hook-key {:arity n :required-by [...]}}`) specifying exact parameter conventions and structural lowering shapes for that frontend's grammar.\n   331\t  2. Structural AST lowering rules marshaling CST operands to those hooks.\n   332\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
