{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg --files collab/yang-base && rg -n -A16 'Everything is a stream|Everything Is a Stream|Everything-is-a-Stream|Everything is a Stream' docs/design/yang.tao.md\"","aggregated_output":"collab/yang-base/1795206225363-architect-yang-preludes-design-r7-review.prompt.md\ncollab/yang-base/1795199200608-architect-yang-preludes-design-r5-jupiter.gpt-6.2-astra.findings.md\n58:> **Everything is a Stream**: Portable I/O and system data flow through append-only streams; hosts may also install explicit local functions that perform direct I/O.\n59-\n60-The elaborator is therefore an observer of a medium: form rows in, explicit term rows out. The checker observes candidate term rows and emits checking results. Neither requires a callback into its producer.\n61-\n62-The associated invariant is exact:\n63-\n64-> Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream.\n65-\n66-Dependencies between stages are represented by input records and their addresses. Requests to another service, if introduced later, must have explicit request and response events. Internal function calls implementing a stage do not require a stream per function invocation.\n67-\n68-This is an application of the existing composition doctrine, not a new orchestration framework.\n69-\n70-### 2.3 Universal data makes inspection and interoperability possible\n71-\n72-The governing axiom states:\n73-\n74-> **Code and State are Datoms**: Code (Universal AST) and runtime execution state are structured datoms, enabling syntax independence and structural reflection.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
