{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '600,675p'\"","aggregated_output":"   600\t---\n   601\t\n   602\t## 8. Portability, content addressing, and malleability\n   603\t\n   604\t### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n   605\t\n   606\t- **ClojureDart AOT literal limits:** Consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.prelude/defquoted`.\n   607\t- **Zero bare integral float literals & zero raw host doubles in guest UAST:** All float operations pass boxed `data/float64` through `yin.vm.float`, avoiding raw host doubles across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt.\n   608\t- **Canonical ordering (`b86bc0e8` invariant):** Recipes, profiles, descriptor maps, and emitted UAST operand sequences sort keys deterministically, guaranteeing byte-identical `dao.jing.cbor` hashes across all 4 hosts.\n   609\t- **No JVM-only reflection:** `yang.core.semantics` and `yang.core.prelude` use pure portable Clojure data transforms.\n   610\t\n   611\t### 8.2 Dependency graph and malleability (`docs/agents/malleability.md`)\n   612\t\n   613\tVerified with `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` (r7: the analyzer's high-degree predicate now counts combined in+out degree ≥ 6, matching this document's rule; `56d17563`). No multi-node cycles and no multi-node SCCs exist. The analyzer prints three SELF-loop warnings (`yang.php.antlr.quoted`, `yang.python.antlr.prelude`, `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude` — macro self-reference in defquoted-family namespaces); these are analyzer-reporting artifacts, not runtime dependency cycles, and are expected to disappear once the defquoted consolidation (P0) lands:\n   614\t\n   615\t```text\n   616\tLayer A (AST & Data Schemas):    yang.core.uast\n   617\tLayer B (Pure Composition):      yang.core.prelude, yang.core.semantics, yang.core.defquoted (P0 host macro ns)\n   618\tLayer C (Registry Admission):    yang.core.prelude-admission, yang.core.module, yang.core.publication\n   619\tLayer D (Guest linker modules,  yrt.effect, yrt.int, yrt.safepoint, yang.call — emitted UAST\n   620\t  emitted from host code):        artifacts consumed at runtime on every backend\n   621\tLayer D' (Host emitter ns for   src/cljc/yang/rt/{effect,int,safepoint}.cljc — clojure namespaces\n   622\t  the D-layer modules):           requiring yang.core.prelude/prelude-admission/core.call\n   623\tLayer E (Language Frontends):    yang.python.antlr.*, yang.typescript.antlr.*, yang.php.antlr.*,\n   624\t                                 yang.clojure.{prelude, core-impl, core-module}\n   625\t```\n   626\t\n   627\tLayer D and D' are deliberately separated in the graph: D is *guest linker modules* (runtime artifacts, host-agnostic by construction); D' is their *host emitter namespaces* (the Clojure namespaces that appear in `bin/analyze-deps.clj`'s graph, requiring Layer B/C seams). Conflating them — as the r5/r6 text did with `yang.rt.*` — mixes runtime identity with emitter identity; D2's settled `yrt.*` naming applies to D, while D' uses the `src/cljc/yang/rt/` path layout.\n   628\t\n   629\t### 8.3 Content-addressing and golden discipline (Clean-Slate)\n   630\t\n   631\tPer the Owner Clean-Slate Directive, regenerate affected golden snapshots cleanly per slice (`P0`–`P4`) and validate correctness via behavioral, 4-host, and CPython/Node/PHP language-oracle parity suites.\n   632\t\n   633\t---\n   634\t\n   635\t## 9. Phased implementation roadmap and acceptance gates\n   636\t\n   637\t**r7 reordering (owner directive D10 — Clojure-first):** the Clojure prelude family is built FIRST; the native py/js/php preludes are untouched by these slices (frozen as landed, zero golden churn), with their `yrt.*`/boxed-float re-architecture deferred to the legacy track (Track B). The original r6 P1–P4 order is superseded; its non-Clojure legs reappear in Track B.\n   638\t\n   639\t| Slice | Scope & deliverables | Golden impact | Concrete acceptance gate |\n   640\t|---|---|---|---|\n   641\t| **P0′ — Composition plumbing & `:pure` host core extensions** | Implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` + `admit-profile` **in `yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3→5 publics, per the §5.2 home rule); add `:pure` host exports (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` across all 4 hosts); consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.defquoted` (dedicated host macro namespace, keeping `yang.core.prelude` at 11 publics); base-prelude emitter recipes record the *current* per-prelude modes as migration truth (`:linear` for `py`, `:balanced` for `php`/`js`/`clj`-family) without changing shapes. | No golden churn for py/js/php (no shape change); new modules get fresh addresses | Closure, missing-manifest, `host-limits`, direct-provenance vs. transitive-footprint tests; 4-host test suite for `data/equiv` (`[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] != [NaN]`, `(keyword nil \"a/b\") != (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`), `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`/`canonical-entries`, and `yin.vm.float` (`2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0`, `0.5 ** -2000 -> :underflow`, `format` `1.0 -> \"1.0\"`); existing py/php oracle suites unchanged-green. |\n   642\t| **P1′ — `yrt.effect` + `yrt.int` with Clojure-only consumers; unified trusted `clj`** | Implement stateless `yrt.effect` (5-slot `data/nth` frames, abortive `raise`/`try-value`/`try-orelse`/`try-finally`/`call-ec`, plus resumable `handle`/`perform` — the frame design anticipates py/php `:depth` accounting but only clj/clj.py exercise it) and `yrt.int`; upgrade `clj` to the unified trusted form (two-step `make-callable`, evaluated `assoc` conditions, `invoke-callable`, `prim-get`/`prim-assoc`, retiring `yang.clojure`'s `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance ops); add `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` for bundled `clj`. **py/js/php preludes untouched** — they keep their own mechanisms. | Refresh `clj`/`yang.clojure` goldens cleanly; py/js/php goldens untouched | `yrt.effect` unit tests (abortive, `finally`, resumable one-shot `handle`/`perform`, cold policy traps) across semantic/stack/register VMs; bundled/linked `yang.clojure` parity under shadowed `(defn get ...)`; independent concurrent `clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. |\n   643\t| **P2′ — Unified `clojure.core` + `yang.clojure` migration** | Publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (pure, `impl-*` prefix, `admit-key?`-guarded) + cell-free `clojure.core` facade; migrate `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core`. | Refresh `yang.clojure` goldens cleanly | Authenticated callable cells returning `false` for all collection predicates; two-step `make-callable` + §8.10.7 condition fidelity; bundled == linked parity for nested `clj → clj.py → clj` unwinds; unified `yang.clojure` suite green. |\n   644\t| **P3′ — Descriptor parameterization + `clj.py` + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (the DEFAULT flip)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics` with UAST-derived arity & role validation; define the python frontend contract; refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks/capabilities from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` (the legacy `py-v1` descriptor pins today's `'py/*` hooks 1:1 — behavior-preserving, gated by the existing CPython oracle suites); publish `clj.py`; flip `yang.python`'s default `runtime-profile` to `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (a revision re-pin in `yang.frontend`). | py goldens regenerate under the descriptor-driven path (legacy descriptor byte-identical outcomes); clojure-core-v1 gets fresh goldens | Legacy-descriptor behavior preservation: full CPython corpus + 4-host parity under `py-v1` pin; end-to-end 4-host `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` suite (numeric/float ops, `:max-bits 53` limit traps, `data/admit-key?` refusals, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-entries` ordering, deterministic `str`/`gensym`); capability refusal tests (typed `except E:`, `genexpr` under `:control/generators :refused`); UAST-derived validation rejecting wrong arity, non-lambda hooks, unqualified hooks, reserved doors, out-of-closure exports. |\n   645\t| **P4′ — Additional N → 1 profiles** | `:yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1` next (descriptor + ts frontend contract); `:yang.php/clojure-core-v1` after. | Fresh goldens per profile | End-to-end parity suites per profile. |\n   646\t| **Track B — Legacy prelude re-architecture (deferred, on demand)** | Migrate the native `py`/`js`/`php` preludes onto `yrt.effect`/`yrt.int`/boxed float (the r6 P1/P4 legs: 4→5-slot contexts, generators via `:gen/yield`, `yrt.safepoint`, `php.sp` integration per its own hooks); undertaken only when legacy demand justifies it. | Refresh py/js/php goldens per migration slice | The r6 P1/P4 gates apply verbatim at that time (generator + safepoint parity, oracle suites). |\n   647\t\n   648\t---\n   649\t\n   650\t## 10. Owner decisions and disposition ledger\n   651\t\n   652\t1. **D10 — Default-profile policy & legacy-track deferral (`Settled — r7 Owner Directive`):** For the parameterized frontends, the **Yin/Clojure profile is the DEFAULT** (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` first; ts/php to follow); the native preludes (`py`/`js`/`php` semantics) become the **Legacy compatibility track** — kept frozen as landed (they already exist at their current content addresses with passing oracle suites), with their `yrt.*`/boxed-float re-architecture deferred to Track B until legacy demand justifies it. The clojure prelude family is built first. Consequence named in §6.1: capability refusals (classes, generators, typed `except`, `with`, kwargs) are the default experience for source written against native semantics; pinning the legacy revision is the escape hatch.\n   653\t2. **D1 — Local mutation model for `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`:**\n   654\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `:mutation/locals :cell` (task-heap cells holding pure persistent Clojure values, matching Python parameter binding, unbound reads, reassignment, loops, and `nonlocal` with per-module `globals` cells). Keep `:single-assignment` as a separate restricted profile.\n   655\t   - *Option B:* `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` only (refuses local reassignment).\n   656\t2. **D2 — Namespace prefix for Layer-2a shared modules:**\n   657\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `yrt.*` (`yrt.effect`, `yrt.int`, `yrt.safepoint`) matching `yang.typescript.md` §17 and `yang.php.md` §9, implemented in Clojure under `src/cljc/yang/rt/*.cljc`.\n   658\t   - *Option B:* `yang.rt.*` for both Clojure namespaces and linker module names.\n   659\t3. **D3 — Python float tagging (r7: moot until Track B — py keeps its tagged `{:py/float}` representation as-frozen; boxed `yin.vm.float` ships for the Clojure path in P0′):**\n   660\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Retain `{:py/float x}` behind a 2-line `py` boundary adapter around boxed `yin.vm.float` through P1 so Python's `1 == 1.0` oracle semantics stay cleanly isolated.\n   661\t   - *Option B:* Migrate Python to untagged `data/float64` carriers in P1.\n   662\t4. **D4 — Golden migration policy (`Settled — Owner Clean-Slate Directive`):**\n   663\t   - Settled in favor of clean golden regeneration per slice (`P0`–`P4`), preserving correctness via behavioral, 4-host, and language-oracle suites rather than frozen-quirk backwards compatibility.\n   664\t5. **D5 — Cross-syntax identifier mapping for Clojure names (`?`, `!`, `-`):**\n   665\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Curated `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` table validated against UAST-derived arity/roles, unit-bound `ambient-resolver`, lexical precedence, and reserved-door bans (`*.impl/*`, `dsg__*`).\n   666\t   - *Option B:* Algorithmic mangling rule (`_q` / `_bang`).\n   667\t6. **D6 — Publishing `clojure.core` and migrating `yang.clojure` (`Settled — Owner Clean-Slate Directive`):**\n   668\t   - Settled in favor of publishing collision-free `clojure.core.impl` + cell-free `clojure.core` AND migrating `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core` in P3 (retiring `yang.clojure`'s legacy `library-for` duplication and unit-local `dsg__call_token` path).\n   669\t7. **D7 — Float exponentiation rounding (r7: `fpow-half` ships in P0′ for the Clojure path; `fpow-base` defers to Track B with the php re-architecture):**\n   670\t   - *Option A (Recommended for P0/P1 — Architect concurred):* Export both `float/fpow-half` and `float/fpow-base` in `yin.vm.float` so `1.1 ** 6` preserves bit-exact parity (`0x1.c585058dde7acp+0` for `py`/`js` vs `0x1.c585058dde7abp+0` for `php`) across existing CPython/Node and PHP language oracles.\n   671\t   - *Option B:* Explicitly approve unifying PHP onto `fpow-half` (or `py`/`js` onto `fpow-base`) and update the affected language's oracle departure ledger.\n   672\t8. **D8 — Three-tier hybrid architecture (`Settled — r6 Owner Directive`):**\n   673\t   - Settled on: (1) `:pure` host value core (`yin.vm.data`, `yin.vm.integer`, boxed `yin.vm.float`, `kind/namespace`) for total, representation-sensitive ops; (2) unified guest algebraic effects (`yrt.effect` over `%capture`) for control flow, generators, and cold error/limit policy traps; (3) minimal VM/stream effects (`cell/*`, `stream/*`, `:module/require`) per ADR 0004.\n   674\t9. **D9 — Focused swappable-prelude scope (`Settled — r6 Owner Directive`):**\n   675\t   - Settled on supporting **Native profiles** (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`) for existing language code plus **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profiles** (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`, future `:yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1`), omitting unnecessary off-diagonal N×M profiles (such as `:yang.clojure/py-v1`) and keeping `yang.clojure` directly on unified `clj` + `clojure.core`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
