{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '333,510p'\"","aggregated_output":"   333\t### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n   334\t\n   335\tA semantics descriptor contains **only portable data** (satisfies `yang.frontend/non-portable-path`):\n   336\t\n   337\t```clojure\n   338\t{:yang.semantics/schema 1\n   339\t :yang.semantics/id :yang.python/clojure-core-v1\n   340\t :yang.semantics/syntax :python\n   341\t :yang.semantics/prelude-module 'clj.py\n   342\t :yang.semantics/ambient-modules\n   343\t [{:module 'yang.call,          :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   344\t  {:module 'yrt.effect,         :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   345\t  {:module 'yrt.int,            :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   346\t  {:module 'clj,                :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   347\t  {:module 'clojure.core.impl,  :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   348\t  {:module 'clojure.core,       :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   349\t  {:module 'clj.py,             :address \"<blake3-address>\"}]\n   350\t\n   351\t :yang.semantics/capabilities\n   352\t {:mutation/locals      :cell          ;; :cell | :single-assignment | :refused\n   353\t  :mutation/subscript   :refused       ;; :supported | :refused\n   354\t  :mutation/attribute   :refused\n   355\t  :mutation/delete      :refused\n   356\t  :scope/global         :supported     ;; per-module globals cell only\n   357\t  :scope/nonlocal       :supported     ;; lexical cells when :mutation/locals is :cell\n   358\t  :calls/positional     :supported\n   359\t  :calls/varargs        :supported     ;; *args\n   360\t  :calls/defaults       :refused\n   361\t  :calls/kwonly         :refused\n   362\t  :calls/kwstar         :refused\n   363\t  :calls/kwargs         :refused\n   364\t  :destructuring/unpack :refused       ;; explicit choice; or :supported via clj.py/unpack\n   365\t  :expr/comprehensions  :supported     ;; eager list/set/dict only; genexpr gated by :control/generators\n   366\t  :control/exceptions   :supported     ;; bare `except:` + `finally` + `raise`\n   367\t  :control/except-typed :refused       ;; class-matched / typed `except ExcType [as e]:` refused when :oo/classes :refused\n   368\t  :control/generators   :refused       ;; gates BOTH `yield`/`yield from` AND generator expressions\n   369\t  :control/with         :refused\n   370\t  :oo/classes           :refused\n   371\t  :modules/import       :ambient-only} ;; :supported | :ambient-only | :refused\n   372\t\n   373\t :yang.semantics/literals\n   374\t {:nil     {:kind :raw, :value nil}\n   375\t  :bool    {:kind :raw}\n   376\t  :str     {:kind :raw}\n   377\t  :float   {:kind :float64-raw}      ;; vs {:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/float}\n   378\t  :int     {:kind :raw-or-call, :safe-max-bits 53, :overflow-op 'clj.py/int-lit}\n   379\t  :unbound {:kind :raw, :value :clj/unbound}}\n   380\t\n   381\t :yang.semantics/hooks\n   382\t {;; Arithmetic & comparisons — ALL namespace-qualified (hygienic, immune to guest shadowing)\n   383\t  :op/add           'clj.py/add\n   384\t  :op/sub           'clj.py/sub\n   385\t  :op/mul           'clj.py/mul\n   386\t  :op/truediv       'clj.py/truediv\n   387\t  :op/floordiv      'clj.py/floordiv\n   388\t  :op/mod           'clj.py/mod\n   389\t  :op/pow           'clj.py/pow\n   390\t  :op/neg           'clj.py/neg\n   391\t  :op/pos           'clj.py/pos\n   392\t  :op/eq            'clj.py/eq\n   393\t  :op/ne            'clj.py/ne\n   394\t  :op/lt            'clj.py/lt\n   395\t  :op/le            'clj.py/le\n   396\t  :op/gt            'clj.py/gt\n   397\t  :op/ge            'clj.py/ge\n   398\t  :op/lnot          'clj.py/lnot\n   399\t  :op/truthy        'clj.py/truthy\n   400\t  ;; Collections, indexing, and comprehension accumulators\n   401\t  :coll/vconj       'clj.py/vconj\n   402\t  :coll/list        'clj.py/list\n   403\t  :coll/tuple       'clj.py/tuple\n   404\t  :coll/set         'clj.py/set-from\n   405\t  :coll/dict        'clj.py/map-from\n   406\t  :coll/getitem     'clj.py/get-item\n   407\t  :comp/list-new    'clj.py/comp-list-new    ;; [init-vec] -> accumulator; py-v1: 'py/list\n   408\t  :comp/list-append 'clj.py/comp-list-append ;; [acc val] -> step result; py-v1: 'py/list-append\n   409\t  :comp/set-new     'clj.py/comp-set-new     ;; [] -> accumulator; py-v1: 'py/set-new\n   410\t  :comp/set-add     'clj.py/comp-set-add     ;; [acc val] -> step result; py-v1: 'py/set-add\n   411\t  :comp/dict-new    'clj.py/comp-dict-new    ;; [] -> accumulator; py-v1: 'py/dict-new\n   412\t  :comp/dict-set    'clj.py/comp-dict-set    ;; [acc k v] -> step result; py-v1: 'py/dict-set\n   413\t  :comp/finish      'clj.py/comp-finish      ;; optional [acc] -> final collection; nil in py-v1\n   414\t  ;; Scopes & bindings\n   415\t  :env/local-get    'clj.py/local-get\n   416\t  :env/global-get   'clj.py/global-get\n   417\t  :env/global-set   'clj.py/global-set\n   418\t  ;; Functions & calls\n   419\t  :fn/arg           'clj.py/arg\n   420\t  :fn/make          'clj.py/make-fn\n   421\t  :fn/call          'clj.py/call\n   422\t  ;; Control flow & unit entry (unit/run-main always takes `[body-fn ambient-resolver]`)\n   423\t  :ctrl/for-each    'clj.py/for-each\n   424\t  :ctrl/try         'clj.py/try\n   425\t  :ctrl/try-finally 'clj.py/try-finally\n   426\t  :ctrl/raise       'clj.py/raise\n   427\t  :ctrl/call-ec     'clj.py/call-ec\n   428\t  :unit/run-main    'clj.py/run-main}\n   429\t\n   430\t ;; Each entry defaults to :kind :cell-accessor (emitted per unit into `ambient-resolver` as\n   431\t ;; `(m/e)`, returning the module's stable task-local authenticated callable cell); optional\n   432\t ;; :kind :value references a non-lambda immutable export directly.\n   433\t :yang.semantics/ambient-projections\n   434\t {\"identity\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'identity,  :kind :cell-accessor}\n   435\t  \"inc\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'inc,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   436\t  \"dec\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'dec,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   437\t  \"str\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'str,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   438\t  \"count\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'count,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n   439\t  \"first\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'first,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n   440\t  \"rest\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'rest,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   441\t  \"second\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'second,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   442\t  \"cons\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'cons,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   443\t  \"conj\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'conj,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   444\t  \"assoc\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'assoc,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n   445\t  \"assoc_in\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'assoc-in,  :kind :cell-accessor}\n   446\t  \"get\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'get,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   447\t  \"get_in\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'get-in,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   448\t  \"update\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'update,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   449\t  \"update_in\" {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'update-in, :kind :cell-accessor}\n   450\t  \"map\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'map,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   451\t  \"filter\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'filter,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   452\t  \"reduce\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'reduce,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   453\t  \"into\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'into,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   454\t  \"keys\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'keys,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   455\t  \"vals\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vals,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   456\t  \"merge\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'merge,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n   457\t  \"is_empty\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'empty?,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   458\t  \"is_nil\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'nil?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   459\t  \"is_map\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'map?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   460\t  \"is_vector\" {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vector?,   :kind :cell-accessor}\n   461\t  \"is_set\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'set?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   462\t  \"ex_info\"   {:module 'clj.py,       :export 'ex-info,   :kind :cell-accessor}}}\n   463\t```\n   464\t\n   465\t### 6.4 Validation, lexical hygiene, authority checks, and parameterization\n   466\t\n   467\t1. **Hygienic generated references (no bare hook symbols):** Every non-nil symbol in `:yang.semantics/hooks` and every executable literal-strategy field (such as `:literals.*.overflow-op`) MUST be namespace-qualified (`:yang.semantics/unqualified-hook` otherwise), so user locals named `conj` or `not` can never capture compiler-emitted calls.\n   468\t2. **Scope-aware precedence for `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`:** Free source identifiers resolve in strict order: (1) lexical scope (`:local`, `:cell`, `:nonlocal`), (2) per-module globals (`:vars` in `globals-cell`), (3) unit-bound ambient resolver (`:ambient` in `globals-cell`, passed via `:unit/run-main`), failing with a guest `NameError` on miss.\n   469\t3. **UAST-derived structural export & reserved-door validation (`validate-descriptor`):**\n   470\t   - Takes `(descriptor frontend-contract artifact-store registry)`, computes the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure**, and inspects every active hook, executable `:literals.*` target, and `:ambient-projections` entry directly against the target manifest's verified `:yin.module/tree` UAST (`wide-app` top-level `(yin/def (quote sym) expr)` definitions):\n   471\t     - **Hooks & executable `:literals.*` targets:** must be namespace-qualified, exported by a module in the selected closure (or required host module checked against `:yin.k/arities`), and defined as a `:lambda` whose parameter count equals `frontend-contract`'s required arity.\n   472\t     - **Ambient projections (`:kind :cell-accessor`):** unique alias names, target `e` is a 0-arg `:lambda` in `m`, and `m` exports 0-arg `init!` and 1-arg `export`.\n   473\t     - **Ambient projections (`:kind :value`):** target `e` is a non-lambda immutable value.\n   474\t     - **Reserved-door ban:** refuses any reference to `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or `*.impl/*` (`clojure.core.impl/*`).\n   475\t   - Any violation fails closed before reading CST packets with `:yang.semantics/invalid-descriptor`.\n   476\t4. **Fail-closed capability enforcement during lowering:** Before lowering any guarded CST construct (`classdef`, `yield_expr`, `genexpr`, `with_stmt`, `del_stmt`, typed `except E:`, kwargs, defaults, subscript mutation), lowering checks the descriptor's capability map (with `genexpr` explicitly gated by `:control/generators`) and emits `{:status :refused :reason :yang.semantics/unsupported-capability :capability <cap> :semantics-id <id> :construct <c> :node <id>}` when disabled.\n   477\t5. **Frontend parameterization (`P2`):** `yang.python.antlr.lower`, `yang.typescript.antlr.lower`, and `yang.php.antlr.lower` read literals, hooks (including 2-arg `:unit/run-main [body-fn ambient-resolver]` and optional `:comp/finish`), capabilities, and projections from `:yang.semantics/descriptor`, preserving full CPython/Node/PHP oracle and 4-host parity under their default profiles.\n   478\t\n   479\t### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\n   480\t\n   481\tNo `yang.frontend` schema change is required (`src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc`):\n   482\t- `:yang.frontend/id` names the frontend syntax + lowering implementation (e.g., `:yang.python/antlr`), and each profile gets an immutable `:yang.frontend/revision` (`\"py-v1\"` vs. `\"clojure-core-v1\"`).\n   483\t- `:yang.frontend/lowering-profile` pins the content address of the `:yang.semantics/descriptor` EDN artifact; `:yang.frontend/runtime-profile` pins the resolved `:yang.prelude/profile` manifest.\n   484\t- Compilation provenance retains the exact `(cst-address, lowering-profile, runtime-profile, unit-address)` tuple.\n   485\t\n   486\t---\n   487\t\n   488\t## 7. Case study: `yang.python` with a `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)\n   489\t\n   490\t### 7.1 Value representation & semantic mapping\n   491\t\n   492\t| Python syntax | Native `py` prelude (`:yang.python/py-v1`) | `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`) |\n   493\t|---|---|---|\n   494\t| `None` | `:py/None` | `nil` |\n   495\t| `True` / `False` | `true` / `false` (numeric as `1`/`0`) | `true` / `false` (**non-numeric**: arithmetic raises guest error) |\n   496\t| `\"abc\"` | `{:py/str \"abc\"}` | `\"abc\"` (raw Yin/UTF-8 string) |\n   497\t| `42` | exact integer (safe raw, else `py/int-lit`) | exact integer (safe raw, else `clj.py/int-lit`) |\n   498\t| `1.5` | `{:py/float <float64>}` | `<float64>` (untagged Jing `data/float64` carrier) |\n   499\t| `[1, 2]` | cell `{:py/type :list :items [1 2]}` | persistent vector `[1 2]` |\n   500\t| `(1, 2)` | `{:py/type :tuple :items [1 2]}` | persistent vector `[1 2]` |\n   501\t| `{\"a\": 1}` | cell `{:py/type :dict ...}` | persistent map `{\"a\" 1}` |\n   502\t| `{1, 2}` | cell `{:py/type :set ...}` | persistent set `#{1 2}` |\n   503\t| `def f(x): ...` | cell `{:py/type :function :code ... :yang.call/entry ...}` | authenticated cell `{:clj.py/type :function :name s :spec spec :yang.call/entry ...}` |\n   504\t| Truthiness | `0`, `\"\"`, `[]`, `{}`, `None`, `False` falsy | Clojure truthiness (`clj.py/truthy`): only `nil` and `false` falsy (`0`, `\"\"`, `[]` are truthy) |\n   505\t| Equality `==` / `!=` | `1 == 1.0 == True`, structural list/dict | `data/equiv`: `1 == 1` `true`, `1 == 1.0` `false`, `1 == True` `false`, `NaN == NaN` `false`, `0.0 == -0.0` `true`, recursive over persistent collections |\n   506\t\n   507\t*Truth-in-advertising invariant:* `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` explicitly declares Clojure truthiness, persistent immutable collections, non-numeric booleans, and kind-strict equality as its support profile — never CPython parity.\n   508\t\n   509\t### 7.2 Portable numeric & collection contract (`clj.py` over `:pure` host core + `yrt.effect`)\n   510\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
