{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '510,599p'\"","aggregated_output":"   510\t\n   511\tBecause the Tier-1 `:pure` host core (`yin.vm.data`, `yin.vm.integer`, `yin.vm.float`) handles all host-representation details natively, `clj.py` becomes a thin, readable adapter:\n   512\t\n   513\t1. **Portable kind classification (`clj.py/num-kind`):**\n   514\t   ```clojure\n   515\t   (if (integer/integer? x)\n   516\t     :int\n   517\t     (if (data/float64? x) :float :other))\n   518\t   ```\n   519\t   Non-numeric operands raise `{:clj.py/error :type-error ...}` via `clj/raise` (in `v1`, string `+` concatenates via `data/str-concat`; `*` is strictly numeric).\n   520\t2. **Int × Int:** Delegates directly to `yin.vm.integer` (`add`, `sub`, `neg`, `mul`, `floor-div-mod`, `pow`, `true-div`, `compare`), checking `b == 0` beforehand (performing `:math/div-zero`) and passing every result through `yrt.int/check-limit` before indexing `[q r]` pairs or chaining into further ops. Negative integer exponents promote `a` via `integer/to-float` + `data/float64` and delegate to `float/neg-pow` (`:half`), performing `:math/overflow` if `:yin.vm.float/underflow` is returned.\n   521\t3. **Float × Float and Mixed Int × Float:**\n   522\t   - Exact ints promote via `(data/float64 (yrt.int/check-limit (clj/rt-ctx) (integer/to-float i)))`.\n   523\t   - `+`, `-`, `*`, unary `-`, unary `+`, `/`, `//`, `%`, `**`, and `<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=` delegate directly to boxed `yin.vm.float` exports (`float/add`, `float/sub`, `float/mul`, `float/neg`, `float/div-checked`, `float/floordiv-mod`, `float/fpow-half`, `float/neg-pow`, `float/compare`) and `integer/compare-float` (via boxed float helper).\n   524\t   - Cold status keywords (`:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, `:yin.vm.float/underflow`, `:yin.vm.float/fractional-exp`, `:yin.vm.float/infinite-exp`) are translated by `clj.py`'s effect handler into guest error maps (`{:clj.py/error :zero-division ...}`, `:overflow`, `:pow-fractional`, `:pow-infinite`) via `yrt.effect/perform` → `clj/raise`.\n   525\t4. **Uniform key admission & equality:**\n   526\t   - **Key/element admission:** Map/set construction and lookup in both `clj.py` and `clojure.core.impl` call `(data/admit-key? k)` once; on `false`, perform `:coll/unsupported-key` (raising `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-key :key k}` or `ex-info`).\n   527\t   - **Equality:** `clj.py/eq` delegates directly to **`data/equiv`**; `clj.py/ne` delegates to `(not (data/equiv a b))`.\n   528\t   - **Deterministic traversal:** Map/set iteration delegates directly to **`data/canonical-entries`**.\n   529\t\n   530\t### 7.3 Python lowering Hook ABI & `clj.py` adapters\n   531\t\n   532\t| Hook key | Frontend ABI signature | `clj.py` implementation |\n   533\t|---|---|---|\n   534\t| `:env/local-get` | `[cell name]` | Reads `(cell/get cell)`; raises guest unbound error if `:clj/unbound`. |\n   535\t| `:env/global-get` | `[globals-cell name]` | Checks `(data/contains? (get g :vars) name)` first; on miss invokes unit-owned `((get g :ambient) name)`; if `:clj/unbound`, raises guest `NameError` map built via evaluated `assoc`. |\n   536\t| `:env/global-set` | `[globals-cell name value]` | Updates `:vars` in `globals-cell` (preserving `:ambient`) and returns `value`. |\n   537\t| `:fn/make` | `[fname spec defaults kwdefaults code]` | Accepts the 5 arguments from `yang.python.antlr.lower/function-value:1870`; delegates to trusted Layer-2b **`clj/make-callable`** (`§7.4`). |\n   538\t| `:fn/call` | `[callee args]` | Delegates to trusted Layer-2b **`clj/invoke-callable`** (`§7.4`). Zero provenance doors inside `clj.py`. |\n   539\t| `:ctrl/try` | `[body handler orelse]` | Calls `yrt.effect/try-orelse` on `(clj/rt-ctx)`. |\n   540\t| `:ctrl/try-finally` | `[body fin]` | Calls `yrt.effect/try-finally` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   541\t| `:ctrl/raise` | `[e]` | Calls `clj/raise` (delegating to `yrt.effect/raise` on `(clj/rt-ctx)`). |\n   542\t| `:ctrl/call-ec` | `[f]` | Calls `yrt.effect/call-ec` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   543\t| `:ctrl/for-each` | `[iterable step-fn]` | Invokes `clojure.core.impl/impl-seq`, `impl-first`, `impl-rest` (backed by `data/canonical-entries` for maps/sets), raises guest error on non-collection iterables, and invokes `step-fn` per element. |\n   544\t| `:comp/list-new`, `:comp/set-new`, `:comp/dict-new` | `[init-vec]`, `[]`, `[]` | Allocates temporary local accumulator cell holding persistent `[]`, `#{}`, or `{}`. |\n   545\t| `:comp/list-append`, `:comp/set-add`, `:comp/dict-set` | `[acc val]`, `[acc val]`, `[acc k v]` | Validates set elements / dict keys via `data/admit-key?`, updates persistent value inside `acc`, returns `nil`. |\n   546\t| `:comp/finish` | `[acc]` *(optional)* | Returns `(cell/get acc)` (omitted/`nil` in `:yang.python/py-v1`). |\n   547\t| `:unit/run-main` | `[body-fn ambient-resolver]` | Calls idempotent `(clj/init!)`, `(clojure.core/init!)`, `(clj.py/init!)`; installs `clj.py`'s cold-effect policy handlers (`:math/*`, `:int/*`, `:coll/unsupported-key`) on `(clj/rt-ctx)`; allocates a fresh per-unit `globals` cell; invokes `(body-fn globals globals-fn)` and returns the value verbatim without stripping `[:yin.k/ok ...]`. |\n   548\t\n   549\t### 7.4 Unified trusted `clj` callable bridge, cross-unit admission, and §8.10.7 validation\n   550\t\n   551\tUnder the Owner Clean-Slate Directive, all Clojure-family §8.10.7 callable/provenance bridging is unified directly into **trusted Layer-2b `clj`** (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc`, requiring `yang.call` and `yrt.effect`) — eliminating both any separate `clj.bridge` module and `yang.clojure`'s legacy `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance code in P3:\n   552\t\n   553\t- `clj` owns the private provenance doors (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, `cell/dsg__provenance`) inside **both** its linked (`module-uast`) and bundled (`uast`) emitters, never exporting them and keeping them strictly out of `yrt.*`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, and `clojure.core`.\n   554\t- `clj` exports collision-free primitive helpers **`clj/prim-get`** and **`clj/prim-assoc`**.\n   555\t- **Source-level callable admission (`clj/admitted-callable?`):** Nested `if` verifying `(data/map? x)`, `(= (get x :type) :cell-ref)`, `(cell/authentic? x)`, `(data/callable? (yang.call/entry x))`, and `(yang.call/eligible? x)`. Plain maps, unauthenticated cell-ref maps, and raw host primitives fail cleanly.\n   556\t- **Two-step cell-backed callable constructor (`clj/make-callable`):** Allocates `owner = (cell/new meta)` first, installs `entry` closing over `owner` via `cell/set!`, and returns `owner`.\n   557\t- **Full 4-step §8.10.7 entry boundary:**\n   558\t  - *Step A:* Verify `(data/map? invocation)` and `(data/callable? (get invocation :yang.call/raise))` (fail operationally otherwise).\n   559\t  - *Step B:* Outside `try-value`, verify `(yang.call/valid-invocation? invocation)` and `(= (get invocation :yang.call/callee) owner)`; build condition evidence via evaluated `assoc` calls and transfer `:yang.call/invalid-invocation` on failure.\n   560\t  - *Step C:* Outside `try-value`, reject unsupported `:yang.call/binding-profile` via evaluated `assoc` evidence and transfer `:yang.call/unsupported-binding`.\n   561\t  - *Step D:* Run argument binding + body inside **`yrt.effect/try-value`** on `(clj/rt-ctx)`. Normal exit restores `(clj/rt-ctx)` and returns the value verbatim; escape inspects private `(cell/dsg__provenance e)` to forward retained protocol conditions without double-wrapping or wrap user escapes via `(yang.call/thrown e)`.\n   562\t- **Call-site boundary (`clj/invoke-callable`):** Checks `clj/admitted-callable?` (minting retained `:yang.call/not-callable` on failure), else calls `yang.call/invoke` with a `raise-exit` that unwraps `:yang.call/thrown` and retains all other protocol conditions via private `cell/dsg__new-provenance`.\n   563\t\n   564\t### 7.5 Two-module portable `clojure.core` contract (`clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`)\n   565\t\n   566\tIn Slice P3, the portable Clojure standard library splits into two Layer-2c linker modules — eliminating store-key collisions against VM primitives while publishing cell-free 0-arg export accessors:\n   567\t\n   568\t1. **`clojure.core.impl` (pure, stateless implementation module — banned from `:ambient-projections`):**\n   569\t   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; zero state cells). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\n   570\t   - **Zero bare primitive store collisions:** Every definition is prefixed `impl-*` (`impl-identity`, `impl-get`, `impl-assoc`, `impl-conj`, etc.), so internal calls to `(get m k)`, `(assoc m k v)`, `(conj xs x)`, `(first xs)`, `(rest xs)`, `(vec xs)`, `(nil? x)`, `(empty? xs)`, `(not b)` resolve directly to VM primitives.\n   571\t   - **Cell-safe collection predicates:** `impl-cell-ref?` ensures authenticated callable cells answer **`false`** to all of `coll?`, `map?`, `set?`, `vector?`, `sequential?`, `seq?`, `list?`, and `reduced?`; `impl-fn?` matches `clj/admitted-callable?` 1-to-1.\n   572\t   - **Host-backed portable operations (zero guest-UAST leak workarounds):**\n   573\t     - `impl-inc`, `impl-dec`, `impl-rem`, `impl-int?`: delegate to `integer/*` + `yrt.int/check-limit` and `float/add`/`float/sub`.\n   574\t     - `impl-not=`: delegates to `(not (data/equiv a b))`.\n   575\t     - `impl-str`: deterministic renderer delegating ints to `integer/format`, floats to `float/format`, keywords/symbols to `kind/namespace` + `kind/name`, maps/sets to `data/canonical-entries`, and authenticated cells to `\"#<fn>\"`.\n   576\t     - `impl-seq`, `impl-first`, `impl-rest`, `impl-vec`, `impl-keys`, `impl-vals`, `impl-reduce`, `impl-map`, `impl-filter`, `impl-remove`, `impl-into`, `impl-merge`, `impl-union`, `impl-difference`: normalize maps/sets via `data/canonical-entries`.\n   577\t     - Map/set mutators and lookups (`impl-assoc`, `impl-get`, `impl-contains?`, `impl-conj`, `impl-disj`, `impl-merge`, `impl-into`, etc.): enforce `data/admit-key?`.\n   578\t     - Explicitly excluded: `var?`, `resolve`, `invoke-value`.\n   579\t2. **Public cell-free facade `clojure.core` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/core_module.cljc`):**\n   580\t   - Requires `clj` and `clojure.core.impl`. Exports only cell-free pure functions at install time: idempotent 0-arg `init!` (building `{sym cell}` with `clj/prim-assoc` and `clj/make-callable`), 1-arg `export` (using `clj/prim-get`), and 0-arg cell-accessor exports `(fn [] (clojure.core/export (quote <name>)))`.\n   581\t   - Dynamic closures (`impl-comp`, `impl-partial`) construct cells via `clj/make-callable`; all dynamic callbacks (`map`, `filter`, `reduce`, `update`, etc.) invoke via `clj/invoke-callable`.\n   582\t   - **Direct `yang.clojure` migration in P3:** Retires `yang.clojure`'s inline `library-for` duplication and unit-local `dsg__call_token` path so there is one unified Clojure runtime.\n   583\t\n   584\t### 7.6 Concrete lowering example\n   585\t\n   586\t```python\n   587\tdef sum_even_squares(xs):\n   588\t    if is_empty(xs):\n   589\t        return 0\n   590\t    evens = filter(lambda n: n % 2 == 0, xs)\n   591\t    squares = map(lambda n: n * n, evens)\n   592\t    return reduce(lambda a, b: a + b, 0, squares)\n   593\t```\n   594\t\n   595\t- `is_empty`, `filter`, `map`, `reduce` resolve via `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` to `clojure.core`'s task-instantiated cell-backed callables.\n   596\t- `%`, `*`, `+`, `==` lower hygienically to `clj.py/mod`, `clj.py/mul`, `clj.py/add`, `clj.py/eq` (backed by `:pure` `yin.vm.integer` / `yin.vm.float` / `data/equiv`).\n   597\t- `lambda n: ...` lowers to `clj.py/make-fn`, producing an authenticated cell-backed `yang.call` callable invoked directly by `clojure.core/filter` and `clojure.core/map`.\n   598\t- `sum_even_squares([1, 2, 3, 4])` evaluates `[1 2 3 4]` → `20` (exact persistent integer), returned verbatim.\n   599\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
