{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i 'balanced|prelude/definitions|runtime-preamble|seq-nodes|prelude' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | tail -78 && nl -ba src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc | sed -n '51,70p;116,148p'\"","aggregated_output":"924:;; like the py/ts/php preludes (`yang.clojure.prelude` carries the reference\n931:;; inline (the linked runtime binds the same family from the prelude); it\n936:  \"The `clj/` continuation family, `[key form]` in prelude notation (each\n937:   form is read with `u/sexp->uast`). Mirrors `yang.clojure.prelude`'s\n2459:           ;; prelude). Its capture-sensitive primitives are the `dsg__*`\n2569:   map stays for the `library-opts`/`unit-opts` fixtures and the prelude's\n3004:;; entry, `clj/run-main` (the `clj` runtime module, yang.clojure.prelude).\n3086:   of it discharges (the runtime preludes avoid this by keeping every\n    51\t(defn wide-app\n    52\t  \"One application whose operands are `nodes` (in order), applied to a lambda\n    53\t   with one parameter per node that returns nil. Every operand runs on the main sequence before the one call, so the\n    54\t   linker's scanners discharge every body read of a sibling or runtime key;\n    55\t   a `then` chain would nest definitions in closure bodies.\"\n    56\t  [nodes]\n    57\t  (let [params (mapv (fn [i] (symbol (str \"%d\" i))) (range (count nodes)))]\n    58\t    (u/mark-tails (apply u/app (u/lam params (u/lit nil)) nodes))))\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(defn module-tree\n    62\t  \"The module tree for `defs` (`[key form]`, already stripped) followed by\n    63\t   the `trailing` UAST nodes.\"\n    64\t  [defs trailing]\n    65\t  (wide-app (into (mapv (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs)\n    66\t                  trailing)))\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\t(defn exports\n    70\t  \"The module's exports: every key of `definitions` in namespace `ns-str`,\n   116\t(defn balanced-definitions->uast\n   117\t  \"Balanced definition-to-UAST emission: each [key form] pair maps to\n   118\t   u/def! and the vector splits at its midpoint, halving sequential depth\n   119\t   versus the linear u/seq-nodes chain. The tree shape is content-addressed:\n   120\t   empty input answers nil, and callers choose balanced versus linear\n   121\t   deliberately - never migrate between the two for style.\"\n   122\t  [defs]\n   123\t  (letfn [(sequence-tree [nodes]\n   124\t            (if (<= (count nodes) 1)\n   125\t              (first nodes)\n   126\t              (let [middle (quot (count nodes) 2)]\n   127\t                (u/then (sequence-tree (subvec nodes 0 middle))\n   128\t                        (sequence-tree (subvec nodes middle))))))]\n   129\t    (sequence-tree (mapv (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs))))\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\t(defn definitions->uast\n   133\t  [defs]\n   134\t  (u/seq-nodes (map (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '293,386p;492,532p;1080,1111p' && nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1372,1399p'\"","aggregated_output":"   293\t {:yang.grammar/package \"<content-address>\"\n   294\t  :yang.grammar/lexer \"RubyLexer\"\n   295\t  :yang.grammar/parser \"RubyParser\"\n   296\t  :yang.grammar/entries\n   297\t  {:module \"program\"\n   298\t   :expression \"expression\"}\n   299\t  :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1}\n   300\t\n   301\t :yang.frontend/options-schema \"<content-address>\"\n   302\t :yang.frontend/lowering-profile \"<content-address>\"\n   303\t :yang.frontend/runtime-profile \"<content-address>\"\n   304\t :yang.frontend/support-profile \"<content-address>\"}\n   305\t```\n   306\t\n   307\tThese names are proposed SPI vocabulary, not existing repository APIs.\n   308\tThe strings identify grammar declarations; they are not classes to\n   309\tinstantiate from untrusted input.\n   310\t\n   311\tHost installation separately binds an admitted package revision to:\n   312\t\n   313\t- Generated JVM classes, JavaScript modules, or Dart libraries.\n   314\t- The corresponding ANTLR runtime.\n   315\t- Any target-specific lexer/parser helper implementation.\n   316\t- A portable lowering implementation, or an explicitly selected lowering\n   317\t  service.\n   318\t- Supplied request, response, control, and diagnostic streams.\n   319\t\n   320\tPortable manifests contain no constructors, function objects,\n   321\tclassloaders, callbacks, or live handles.\n   322\t\n   323\t### 3.2 Protocol shape\n   324\t\n   325\tThe contract a frontend satisfies, written as Clojure pseudocode. Every\n   326\tname here is proposed vocabulary that organizes the four parts of 3.1 and\n   327\tthe lowering step of 3.5; none of it exists in the repository today.\n   328\t\n   329\t```clojure\n   330\t;; A frontend is a value: its manifest plus the installed binding the\n   331\t;; composition attached to it. Nothing here is a namespace or a global.\n   332\t\n   333\t(defprotocol YangFrontend\n   334\t  ;; 3.1 part 1 and 2: grammar package and syntax export profile.\n   335\t  (grammar-manifest [this]\n   336\t    \"The :yang.frontend/grammar map: package address, lexer and parser\n   337\t     declarations, entry rules, export profile.\")\n   338\t  (support-profile [this]\n   339\t    \"The 3.4 claims: syntax, semantics, lowering, stdlib, host and effect\n   340\t     requirements, REPL completeness, incremental parsing.\")\n   341\t  ;; REPL completeness probe (3.4, 5.3). Returns\n   342\t  ;; :complete, :incomplete, or :invalid. Optional; absent means the\n   343\t  ;; composition must use an explicit submit action.\n   344\t  (completeness [this source-snapshot options])\n   345\t  ;; 3.1 part 3: the semantic frontend as a stepped interpreter.\n   346\t  ;; Consumes a sealed, validated CST packet and an explicit compilation\n   347\t  ;; environment. Returns the 3.5 transition result.\n   348\t  (lowering-step [this state observed-input budget])\n   349\t  ;; 3.1 part 4: the runtime profile, resolved to prelude addresses.\n   350\t  (runtime-profile [this]))\n   351\t\n   352\t;; The transition result of lowering-step (3.5):\n   353\t;; {:yang.lower/state     successor-state\n   354\t;;  :yang.lower/staged    [ephemeral Universal AST maps or packets]\n   355\t;;  :yang.lower/status    :running | :done | :rejected | :blocked}\n   356\t\n   357\t;; Registration constructs a new catalog value (3.3):\n   358\t;; (install catalog validated-manifest installed-binding) => catalog'\n   359\t```\n   360\t\n   361\tThe Clojure frontend implements this same contract through its existing\n   362\treader. The open SPI does not require every frontend to use ANTLR.\n   363\t\n   364\t### 3.3 Registration and selection\n   365\t\n   366\tRegistration means constructing a new catalog value:\n   367\t\n   368\t```clojure\n   369\tcatalog' = install(catalog, validated-manifest, installed-binding)\n   370\t```\n   371\t\n   372\tThis is not namespace-load registration or mutation of a global\n   373\tregistry. There is no closed language registry anywhere in Yang core.\n   374\t\n   375\tThe composition supplies the catalog to the compiler coordinator. A\n   376\trequest selects a frontend revision and dialect explicitly. Filename\n   377\textensions and content detection can propose a frontend, but ambiguous\n   378\tdetection produces a diagnostic or a choice record rather than silently\n   379\tchoosing.\n   380\t\n   381\tIn-flight requests pin a catalog snapshot. Installing a newer frontend\n   382\tdoes not change their behavior.\n   383\t\n   384\tA missing frontend, missing entry rule, incompatible SPI, unknown required\n   385\toption, or unavailable parser implementation produces a qualified\n   386\tcompiler outcome. None causes automatic dependency downloading or\n   492\t+---------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------+\n   493\t| Consumer host | Local parser implementation   | Alternative              |\n   494\t+===============+===============================+==========================+\n   495\t| JVM / CLJ     | Generated Java parser in an   | Configured parsing       |\n   496\t|               | isolated worker or worker     | service                  |\n   497\t|               | process                       |                          |\n   498\t+---------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------+\n   499\t| Node / CLJS   | Generated JavaScript parser   | Local sidecar or remote  |\n   500\t|               | in a worker; TypeScript       | service                  |\n   501\t|               | compiled at build             |                          |\n   502\t+---------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------+\n   503\t| Dart / CLJD   | Generated Dart parser (the    | Sidecar where supported, |\n   504\t|               | local implementation for      | or a remote service;     |\n   505\t|               | Python since 2026-10-17; a    | otherwise unsupported    |\n   506\t|               | grammar without a Dart helper | outcome                  |\n   507\t|               | answers `unavailable-parser`) |                          |\n   508\t+---------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------+\n   509\t```\n   510\t\n   511\tA CLJD application can compile through a service without bundling ANTLR.\n   512\tIt can also consume previously compiled rows without any parser.\n   513\t\n   514\tFull offline local compilation on all three hosts requires validated\n   515\tparser artifacts for all three. Service-based portability must not be\n   516\tadvertised as offline portability.\n   517\t\n   518\tSource is sent only to an endpoint supplied by the composition.\n   519\tUnavailability does not trigger an undisclosed remote fallback.\n   520\t\n   521\t### 4.2 Grammar discipline and per-host generation\n   522\t\n   523\tGrammars live in `.g4` files. Prefer grammars with **zero\n   524\ttarget-specific embedded actions**, so one grammar source generates for\n   525\tevery host. Where indentation or lexical ambiguities require helpers,\n   526\tversion and test those helpers per target. The grammars-v4 project\n   527\texpresses an action-free expectation, not a guarantee that every grammar\n   528\tworks unchanged on every target (https://github.com/antlr/grammars-v4).\n   529\t\n   530\tGenerate parsers during reproducible builds, not while admitting source\n   531\tprograms. One grammar is generated once per host target:\n   532\t\n  1080\t\n  1081\t### 7.4 Provenance and fingerprinting\n  1082\t\n  1083\tUse the repository's occurrence coordinate:\n  1084\t\n  1085\t```clojure\n  1086\t[[:source program-medium batch-token member-index]\n  1087\t root-address\n  1088\t structural-path]\n  1089\t```\n  1090\t\n  1091\tThis is separate from the original source-file revision. Record the link\n  1092\tfrom the program admission occurrence to the source snapshot and\n  1093\tfrontend profile.\n  1094\t\n  1095\tA compilation derivation record pins source, grammar, normalization,\n  1096\tlowering, runtime profile, dependency snapshot, and output roots. Its\n  1097\taddress is published through ordinary ledger datoms. This record is the\n  1098\tfingerprint of a compilation: two compilations with the same pinned\n  1099\tinputs produce the same record address and the same output root\n  1100\taddresses.\n  1101\t\n  1102\tContent addresses occupy `v`, not `e`. The transactor owns persistent\n  1103\tlocal IDs and transaction time. Optional AST datom projections remain\n  1104\tregenerable query views and never become the load identity.\n  1105\t\n  1106\t---\n  1107\t\n  1108\t## 8. Semantic lowering per paradigm\n  1109\t\n  1110\tThe language list in this section is non-exhaustive. Each subsection is\n  1111\ta reference mapping from one paradigm to the Universal AST; a new\n  1372\t  refused child's store is published.\n  1373\t- **`linked` lifts the exports; each receiver relocates them.** A\n  1374\t  child's store holds closures whose code coordinates are the child's:\n  1375\t  a stack or register closure carries a body pc into the child's held\n  1376\t  segment and no image identity; a semantic closure carries a local\n  1377\t  segment id minted by the child's loader. Published as they are, those\n  1378\t  coordinates are meaningless in the parent, so bindings cross the\n  1379\t  child-to-parent boundary the way a continuation crosses any boundary:\n  1380\t  by lift and lower. The `linked` transition is four acts: acts 1\n  1381\t  and 2 run once, at `validated`; acts 3 and 4 run once per\n  1382\t  receiving task -- the parent at `linked`, and each waiter or later\n  1383\t  requirer at its own restore.\n  1384\t  Before act 1, every present `:yin.module/requires` dependency must have\n  1385\t  the halted child's linked entry at its pinned manifest address.\n  1386\t  Present-and-unequal refuses `:dependency-pin-mismatch` with `:module`,\n  1387\t  `:name`, `:pinned`, and `:linked`, choosing the first mismatch by name\n  1388\t  string order. Absence is permitted at install for deferred dependencies.\n  1389\t  At each receive (child inheritance and parent acts 3 and 4), the registry\n  1390\t  pin invariant checks both existing manifests' pins for the incoming name\n  1391\t  and the incoming manifest's pins for held names, before any attachment or\n  1392\t  lowering. Thus a deferred name can only bind at its pinned address.\n  1393\t  Nothing is published on refusal; every waiter receives the refusal.\n  1394\t  1. *The child's export slice is lifted* to UCF's portable encoding\n  1395\t     (section 7.5.1, amended below): each closure becomes a\n  1396\t     `:yin.k/closure` marker naming its **origin image** and its entry\n  1397\t     relative to that image, with its captured values encoded\n  1398\t     recursively; every other value encodes by the same grammar. The\n  1399\t     origin is not assumed to be the module's own image: a closure the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
