       shared ruling of yang.typescript.md section 2; the kind\\\\\\\\n    15\\\\\\\\t                     test is `php/kind`, never a second tag. The prelude\\\\\\\\n    16\\\\\\\\t                     holds no integral float literal (JS reads 1.0 as 1):\\\\\\\\n    17\\\\\\\\t                     floats are built with `data/float64` or computed, and\\\\\\\\n    18\\\\\\\\t                     host arithmetic only ever sees `data/float-value`\\\\\\\\n    19\\\\\\\\t     string          a host string whose every char is one byte (a latin-1\\\\\\\\n    20\\\\\\\\t                     carrier); the lowering resolves literal text to bytes\\\\\\\\n    21\\\\\\\\t     bool            host true / false\\\\\\\\n    22\\\\\\\\t     null            :php/null\\\\\\\\n    23\\\\\\\\t     array           {:php/type :array :index {key value} :order [key ...]\\\\\\\\n    24\\\\\\\\t                     :next-index n}: a persistent ordered map; keys are\\\\\\\\n    25\\\\\\\\t                     ints or strings (`php/array-key`); `:next-index` is\\\\\\\\n    26\\\\\\\\t                     absent until the first integer key is written\\\\\\\\n    27\\\\\\\\t     error object    {:php/type :obj :class name :ord n :props {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    28\\\\\\\\t                     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"code\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"previous\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\n    29\\\\\\\\t     function        a cell {:php/type :function :name s :code (fn [args])\\\\\\\\n    30\\\\\\\\t                             :yang.call/entry (fn [invocation])}\\\\\\\\n    31\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    32\\\\\\\\t   Runtime state is allocated by `php/init!`, once per task, under the slot\\\\\\\\n    33\\\\\\\\t   `php.rt/state` (the literal `:php/uninit` until `php/init!` flips it to\\\\\\\\n    34\\\\\\\\t   `:php/ready` as its last write):\\\\\\\\n    35\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/ctx            the dynamic context {:handlers :depth :base :frame}\\\\\\\\n    36\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/out            a cell holding the buffer stack, a vector of\\\\\\\\n    37\\\\\\\\t                           buffers, each a vector of byte-string chunks;\\\\\\\\n    38\\\\\\\\t                           `php/echo` conjs onto the last buffer, the\\\\\\\\n    39\\\\\\\\t                           bottom buffer is never popped\\\\\\\\n    40\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/globals        a cell holding the plain array of section 10.1\\\\\\\\n    41\\\\\\\\t                           (`$GLOBALS`), `(php/empty-array)` initially\\\\\\\\n    42\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/functions      a cell holding a map of lower-cased name to\\\\\\\\n    43\\\\\\\\t                           function cell; builtins are pre-seeded\\\\\\\\n    44\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/classes        a cell holding a map of class name to class record\\\\\\\\n    45\\\\\\\\t                           (the Throwable hierarchy, data only)\\\\\\\\n    46\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/next-ord       a cell, the per-task object ordinal\\\\\\\\n    47\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/next-cell      a cell, the per-task counted-cell id (`:id`)\\\\\\\\n    48\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/request        a cell holding the explicit request record\\\\\\\\n    49\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/response       a cell holding ordered response records\\\\\\\\n    50\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/headers-sent, php.rt/status   output state and the response status\\\\\\\\n    51\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/error-handler  a cell, :php/null or a callable\\\\\\\\n    52\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/error-handlers a cell holding previous handlers for restoration\\\\\\\\n    53\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/error-reporting a cell, the mask (E_ALL initially)\\\\\\\\n    54\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/diag           a cell, the vector of diagnostic records\\\\\\\\n    55\\\\\\\\t     php.rt/int-max, php.rt/int-min   exact integers computed in `init!`,\\\\\\\\n    56\\\\\\\\t                           never literals (literals past 2^53 are not\\\\\\\