\\n  2440\\\\\\\\thandler source and **confirmed by the oracle before the slice that claims it\\\\\\\\n  2441\\\\\\\\tlands**. After landing, a disagreement between a row and the pinned PHP CLI is\\\\\\\\n  2442\\\\\\\\ta defect of the row, never of the fixture. A finding that a claimed row\\\\\\\\n  2443\\\\\\\\tcontradicts Zend blocks landing of any slice whose support profile includes\\\\\\\\n  2444\\\\\\\\tthat row until either the row is corrected (and its fixture regenerated from\\\\\\\\n  2445\\\\\\\\tthe oracle), or the Architect explicitly moves the behaviour to section 17.2\\\\\\\\n  2446\\\\\\\\tas a restricted corner with a departure fixture whose expected value is the\\\\\\\\n  2447\\\\\\\\trecorded deviation, with the owner's acceptance when the corner touches a\\\\\\\\n  2448\\\\\\\\tPhase 3 exit criterion. Regenerating a fixture to match an incorrect row is\\\\\\\\n  2449\\\\\\\\tforbidden: oracle fixtures pin behaviour; they do not legitimize a\\\\\\\\n  2450\\\\\\\\tcontradictory normative rule.\\\\\\\\n  2451\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  2452\\\\\\\\tThe landing gate is therefore: every claimed-row fixture equals the oracle;\\\\\\\\n  2453\\\\\\\\tevery corner's departure fixture equals its recorded deviation; no fixture\\\\\\\\n  2454\\\\\\\\tfailure is unclassified. A new finding lands in one of four bins, in blocking\\\\\\\\n  2455\\\\\\\\torder:\\\\\\\\n  2456\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  2457\\\\\\\\t1. a defect in a claimed row (blocks);\\\\\\\\n  2458\\\\\\\\t2. a missing row required by an exit criterion or the C4 profile (blocks);\\\\\\\\nnl: test/yang/php/antlr/p9_test.clj: No such file or directory\\\\\\\\n5126:   [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ErrorException\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :class \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Exception\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" []] [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"JsonException\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :class \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Exception\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" []]\\\\\\\\n5168:  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ErrorException: Exception's members, the `severity` property, its own\\\\\\\\n5174:                {:name mn, :lc (s