engine.cljc | sed -n '2735,2768p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | sed -n '298,340p;390,420p'; nl -ba docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '492,516p;4380,4429p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"     1\\\\\\\\t(ns yang.safepoint\\\\\\\\n     2\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The safepoint stage (Architect safepoint-interpreter design, slice 1): a\\\\\\\\n     3\\\\\\\\t   pure rewrite of a canonical program tree `A` into a derived tree `A'` that\\\\\\\\n     4\\\\\\\\t   applies a hook at every frontend-marked site the profile maps.\\\\\\\\n     5\\\\\\\\t   Language-neutral: it knows the Universal AST row grammar and the\\\\\\\\n     6\\\\\\\\t   frontend-metadata side table, nothing about any guest language. The hooks'\\\\\\\\n     7\\\\\\\\t   meaning lives in a per-language hook prelude; the evaluator never learns\\\\\\\\n     8\\\\\\\\t   what a safepoint is.\\\\\\\\n     9\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    10\\\\\\\\t   - A site is a `:lambda` occurrence the frontend marked with `:yang/site`\\\\\\\\n    11\\\\\\\\t     metadata, which projection puts in the side table as\\\\\\\\n    12\\\\\\\\t     `[origin root path :yang/site kind]`. A profile `{kind hook-symbol}`\\\\\\\\n    13\\\\\\\\t     selects sites; a kind it omits is not inserted.\\\\\\\\n    14\\\\\\\\t   - Insertion prefixes the site's body with an ordinary `:application` of\\\\\\\\n    15\\\\\\\\t     the hook, sequenced through a lambda whose one binder is `binder`, in a\\\\\\\\n    16\\\\\\\\t     reserved namespace: no new tag, no gensym counter. An exit kind\\\\\\\\n    17\\\\\\\\t     (`exit-kinds`: `:return` at `:call` sites) wraps the body instead: its\\\\\\\\n    18\\\\\\\\t     hook is applied to the body's value, so it runs on normal exit only.\\\\\\\\n    19\\\\\\\\t   - A mark's value is a kind, or a vector `[kind datum ...]`: the data\\\\\\\\n    20\\\\\\\\t     (a function's name and line, a statement's line) are literals the\\\\\\\\n    21\\\\\\\\t     frontend knows and the derived tree may need. A profile entry is a\\\\\\\\n    22\\\\\\\\t     hook symbol, or `{:hook symbol :operands true}` to apply the hook to\\\\\\\\n    23\\\\\\\\t     the mark's data. A statement kind (`statement-kinds`: `:line`) marks\\\\\\\\n    24\\\\\\\\t     any node, not a lambda; its hook is applied before the node, which\\\\\\\\n    25\\\\\\\\t     is sequenced after it.\\\\\\\\n    26\\\\\\\\t   - Every tail mark is stripped and recomputed over the whole derived tree\\\\\\\\n    27\\\\\\\\t     (`yang.tails`): a wrapped body's old tail calls would otherwise skip\\\\\\\\n    28\\\\\\\\t     its wrapper. With no site selected `A'` is `A`, row for row.\\\\\\\\n    29\\\\\\\\t   - `A` is never modified. Names, the ledger and publication refer to it;\\\\\\\\n    30\\\\\\\\t     the link is a `:derive` record with input `A`, output `A'`, function\\\\\\\\n    31\\\\\\\\t     `function`, and a profile pinning the hook map and the address of the\\\\\\\\n    32\\\\\\\\t     sorted site set. Insertion is deterministic, so a repeat writes the\\\\\\\\n    33\\\\\\\\t     same record.\\\\\\\\n    34\\\\\\\\t   - `A'` leaves on the stage's own medium in a projected envelope whose\\\\\\\\n    35\\\\\\\\t     batch token is the record's address, so its occurrence origin is an\\\\\\\\n    36\\\\\\\\t     ordinary `[:source medium' token 0]`. No side table is copied: an `A'`\\\\\\\\n    37\\\\\\\\t     node's facts are a join back to `A` through the site set.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    38\\\\\\\\t  (:require\\\\\\\\n    39\\\\\\\\t    [dao.jing :as jing]\\\\\\\\n    40\\\\\\\\t    [yang.stage :as stage]\\\\\\\\n    41\\\\\\\\t    [yang.tails :as tails]\\\\\\\\n    42\\\\\\\\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\\\\\\\\n    43\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    44\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    45\\\\\\\\t(def binder\\\\\\\\n    46\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The parameter of every inserted sequencing lambda.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    47\\\\\\\\t  'yang.safepoint/_)\\\\\\\\n    48\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    49\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    50\\\\\\\\t(def function\\\\\\\\n    51\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The `:yin.ledger/function` of a safepoint derivation.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    52\\\\\\\\t  :yang.safepoint/insert)\\\\\\\\n    53\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    54\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    55\\\\\\\\t(def site-key\\\\\\\\n    56\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The frontend-metadata key a site mark travels under.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    57\\\\\\\\t  :yang/site)\\\\\\\\n    58\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    59\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    60\\\\\\\\t(defn sites\\\\\\\\n    61\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`{path mark}` (a kind, or `[kind datum ...]`) of every site marked in the frontend-metadata relation\\\\\\\\n    62\\\\\\\\t   `metadata` at occurrence `origin` of tree `root`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    63\\\\\\\\t  [metadata origin root]\\\\\\\\n    64\\\\\\\\t  (into {}\\\\\\\\n    65\\\\\\\\t        (keep (fn [[o r path k v]]\\\\\\\\n    66\\\\\\\\t                (when (and (= o origin) (= r root) (= k site-key))\\\\\\\\n    67\\\\\\\\t                  [path v])))\\\\\\\\n    68\\\\\\\\t        metadata))\\\\\\\\n    69\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    70\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    71\\\\\\\\t(defn site-set\\\\\\\\n    72\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The selected sites as a sorted vector of `[path mark]`, a mark a kind or `[kind datum ...]`, in an order every\\\\\\\\n    73\\\\\\\\t   host computes alike.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    74\\\\\\\\t  [selected]\\\\\\\\n    75\\\\\\\\t  (vec (sort-by pr-str (map vec selected))))\\\\\\\\n    76\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    77\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    78\\\\\\\\t(def exit-kinds\\\\\\\\n    79\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Exit kind -> the entry kind whose sites it wraps. An exit hook is applied\\\\\\\\n    80\\\\\\\\t   to the value of the site's body, so it runs after a normal exit and its\\\\\\\\n    81\\\\\\\\t   answer is the body's value; an escape out of the body skips it.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    82\\\\\\\\t  {:return :call})\\\\\\\\n    83\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    84\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    85\\\\\\\\t(def statement-kinds\\\\\\\\n    86\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Kinds whose sites are any node, not a lambda: the hook runs before the\\\\\\\\n    87\\\\\\\\t   node, and the node's value is the site's.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    88\\\\\\\\t  #{:line})\\\\\\\\n    89\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    90\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    91\\\\\\\\t(defn- mark-kind\\\\\\\\n    92\\\\\\\\t  [mark]\\\\\\\\n    93\\\\\\\\t  (if (vector? mark) (first mark) mark))\\\\\\\\n    94\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    95\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    96\\\\\\\\t(defn- entry-hook\\\\\\\\n    97\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The `{:hook sym :operands [literal ...]}` of profile entry `entry` at a\\\\\\\\n    98\\\\\\\\t   site marked `mark`, or nil.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    99\\\\\\\\t  [entry mark]\\\\\\\\n   100\\\\\\\\t  (when entry\\\\\\\\n   101\\\\\\\\t    (if (map? entry)\\\\\\\\n   102\\\\\\\\t      {:hook (:hook entry),\\\\\\\\n   103\\\\\\\\t       :operands (when (:operands entry) (vec (rest mark)))}\\\\\\\\n   104\\\\\\\\t      {:hook entry})))\\\\\\\\n   105\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   106\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   107\\\\\\\\t(defn- site-hooks\\\\\\\\n   108\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`{:enter h :exit h}` (either absent), each an `entry-hook`, for a site\\\\\\\\n   109\\\\\\\\t   marked `mark` under `profile`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   110\\\\\\\\t  [profile mark]\\\\\\\\n   111\\\\\\\\t  (let [kind (mark-kind mark)\\\\\\\\n   112\\\\\\\\t        exit (some (fn [[x entry]] (when (= entry kind) (get profile x)))\\\\\\\\n   113\\\\\\\\t                   exit-kinds)]\\\\\\\\n   114\\\\\\\\t    (cond-> {}\\\\\\\\n   115\\\\\\\\t      (get profile kind) (assoc :enter (entry-hook (get profile kind) mark))\\\\\\\\n   116\\\\\\\\t      (and (map? (get profile kind)) (:sequence (get profile kind)))\\\\\\\\n   117\\\\\\\\t      (assoc :sequence? true)\\\\\\\\n   118\\\\\\\\t      exit (assoc :exit (entry-hook exit mark)))))\\\\\\\\n   119\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   120\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   121\\\\\\\\t(defn- hook-application\\\\\\\\n   122\\\\\\\\t  [{:keys [hook operands]} args]\\\\\\\\n   123\\\\\\\\t  {:type :application,\\\\\\\\n   124\\\\\\\\t   :operator {:type :variable, :name hook},\\\\\\\\n   125\\\\\\\\t   :operands (into (mapv (fn [x] {:type :literal, :value x}) operands) args)})\\\\\\\\n   126\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   127\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   128\\\\\\\\t(defn- sequence-hook\\\\\\\\n   129\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`node` evaluated after `hook` is applied.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   130\\\\\\\\t  [node hook]\\\\\\\\n   131\\\\\\\\t  {:type :application,\\\\\\\\n   132\\\\\\\\t   :operator {:type :lambda, :params [binder], :body node},\\\\\\\\n   133\\\\\\\\t   :operands [(hook-application hook [])]})\\\\\\\\n   134\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   135\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   136\\\\\\\\t(defn- prefix-hook\\\\\\\\n   137\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Lambda `node` with `hook` applied before its body runs.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   138\\\\\\\\t  [node hook]\\\\\\\\n   139\\\\\\\\t  (assoc node\\\\\\\\n   140\\\\\\\\t         :body (sequence-hook (:body node) hook)))\\\\\\\\n   141\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   142\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   143\\\\\\\\t(defn- wrap-hook\\\\\\\\n   144\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Lambda `node` with `hook` applied to its body's value.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   145\\\\\\\\t  [node hook]\\\\\\\\n   146\\\\\\\\t  (assoc node :body (hook-application hook [(:body node)])))\\\\\\\\n   147\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   148\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   149\\\\\\\\t(defn- rewrite\\\\\\\\n   150\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The map AST `ast` with each `{path {:enter h :exit h}}` site's exit hook\\\\\\\\n   151\\\\\\\\t   wrapped around its body and its entry hook prefixed. Throws when a site\\\\\\\\n   152\\\\\\\\t   names no node, or a node that is not a lambda.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   153\\\\\\\\t  [ast hooks]\\\\\\\\n   154\\\\\\\\t  (let [seen (volatile! #{})]\\\\\\\\n   155\\\\\\\\t    (letfn [(walk\\\\\\\\n   156\\\\\\\\t              [node path]\\\\\\\\n   157\\\\\\\\t              (let [slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (:type node))\\\\\\\\n   158\\\\\\\\t                    node (reduce\\\\\\\\n   159\\\\\\\\t                           (fn [n [j [field kind]]]\\\\\\\\n   160\\\\\\\\t                             (let [pos (+ j 2)]\\\\\\\\n  2735\\\\\\\\t             :value (:val effect),\\\\\\\\n  2736\\\\\\\\t             :blocked? false})\\\\\\\\n  2737\\\\\\\\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n  2738\\\\\\\\t                handler (module/get-effect-handler (:modules state)\\\\\\\\n  2739\\\\\\\\t                                                   (:effect effect))]\\\\\\\\n  2740\\\\\\\\t            (if handler\\\\\\\\n  2741\\\\\\\\t              (handler s' effect (assoc opts :id id))\\\\\\\\n  2742\\\\\\\\t              (fail \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Unknown effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" {:effect (:effect effect)}))))]\\\\\\\\n  2743\\\\\\\\t    (update result\\\\\\\\n  2744\\\\\\\\t            :state\\\\\\\\n  2745\\\\\\\\t            (fn [result-state]\\\\\\\\n  2746\\\\\\\\t              (telemetry/emit-snapshot (assoc result-state\\\\\\\\n  2747\\\\\\\\t                                              :value (:value result))\\\\\\\\n  2748\\\\\\\\t                                       :effect\\\\\\\\n  2749\\\\\\\\t                                       {:effect-type (:effect effect)})))))\\\\\\\\n  2750\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  2751\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  2752\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n  2753\\\\\\\\t;; Program Cache Machinery\\\\\\\\n  2754\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n  2755\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  2756\\\\\\\\t(def default-compiled-cache-limit 8)\\\\\\\\n  2757\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  2758\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  2759\\\\\\\\t(defn build-program-index\\\\\\\\n  2760\\\\\\\\t  [datoms]\\\\\\\\n  2761\\\\\\\\t  (group-by first (vec datoms)))\\\\\\\\n  2762\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  2763\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  2764\\\\\\\\t(defn frame-versions\\\\\\\\n  2765\\\\\\\\t  [frame]\\\\\\\\n  2766\\\\\\\\t  (loop [f frame\\\\\\\\n  2767\\\\\\\\t         acc #{}]\\\\\\\\n  2768\\\\\\\\t    (if (map? f)\\\\\\\\n   298\\\\\\\\t  effect/make)\\\\\\\\n   299\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   300\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   301\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n   302\\\\\\\\t;; The `stream` module\\\\\\\\n   303\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n   304\\\\\\\\t;;\\\\\\\\n   305\\\\\\\\t;; These are pure effect constructors. They touch no stream: Yin source calls\\\\\\\\n   306\\\\\\\\t;; them through the module system, they return effects, and the engine\\\\\\\\n   307\\\\\\\\t;; interprets those. `take!` is deliberately absent: destructive read is one\\\\\\\\n   308\\\\\\\\t;; reader's progress and every other reader's data loss, and a v2 `take!` would\\\\\\\\n   309\\\\\\\\t;; need the reader-position-in-the-medium the contract retired.\\\\\\\\n   310\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   311\\\\\\\\t(defn make\\\\\\\\n   312\\\\\\\\t  ([] (make nil))\\\\\\\\n   313\\\\\\\\t  ([cap] (make-effect :stream/make {:capacity cap})))\\\\\\\\n   314\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   315\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   316\\\\\\\\t(defn put!\\\\\\\\n   317\\\\\\\\t  [s v]\\\\\\\\n   318\\\\\\\\t  (make-effect :stream/put {:stream s, :val v}))\\\\\\\\n   319\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   320\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   321\\\\\\\\t(defn cursor\\\\\\\\n   322\\\\\\\\t  [s]\\\\\\\\n   323\\\\\\\\t  (make-effect :stream/cursor {:stream s}))\\\\\\\\n   324\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   325\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   326\\\\\\\\t(defn next!\\\\\\\\n   327\\\\\\\\t  [c]\\\\\\\\n   328\\\\\\\\t  (make-effect :stream/next {:cursor c}))\\\\\\\\n   329\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   330\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   331\\\\\\\\t(defn poll!\\\\\\\\n   332\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`next!` that never parks: `blocked` is the value `:dao.stream/blocked`.\\\\\\\\n   333\\\\\\\\t   It is its own effect kind, so a callee whose profile omits it cannot\\\\\\\\n   334\\\\\\\\t   observe whether a read would have waited.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   335\\\\\\\\t  [c]\\\\\\\\n   336\\\\\\\\t  (make-effect :stream/poll {:cursor c}))\\\\\\\\n   337\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   338\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   339\\\\\\\\t(defn close!\\\\\\\\n   340\\\\\\\\t  [s]\\\\\\\\n   390\\\\\\\\t(defn get-cell\\\\\\\\n   391\\\\\\\\t  [c]\\\\\\\\n   392\\\\\\\\t  (make-effect :cell/get {:cell c}))\\\\\\\\n   393\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   394\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   395\\\\\\\\t(defn set-cell!\\\\\\\\n   396\\\\\\\\t  [c v]\\\\\\\\n   397\\\\\\\\t  (make-effect :cell/set! {:cell c, :val v}))\\\\\\\\n   398\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   399\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   400\\\\\\\\t(def cell-module\\\\\\\\n   401\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The `cell` module definition. Registering it is a composition step.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   402\\\\\\\\t  {'new new-cell, 'get get-cell, 'set! set-cell!})\\\\\\\\n   403\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   404\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   405\\\\\\\\t(def cell-profiles\\\\\\\\n   406\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"UCF 7.5.2 profiles for the `cell` module's bindings: each an\\\\\\\\n   407\\\\\\\\t   `:effectful` pure effect constructor declaring its one effect kind.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   408\\\\\\\\t  {'new (vm/primitive-profile 'new :effectful [1] #{:cell/new} :none)\\\\\\\\n   409\\\\\\\\t   'get (vm/primitive-profile 'get :effectful [1] #{:cell/get} :none)\\\\\\\\n   410\\\\\\\\t   'set! (vm/primitive-profile 'set! :effectful [2] #{:cell/set!} :none)})\\\\\\\\n   411\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   412\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   413\\\\\\\\t(defn register-cell-module\\\\\\\\n   414\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Return registry with the `cell` module registered.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   415\\\\\\\\t  [registry]\\\\\\\\n   416\\\\\\\\t  (register-host-module registry 'cell cell-module cell-profiles))\\\\\\\\n   417\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   418\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   419\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n   420\\\\\\\\t;; Built-in effect handlers\\\\\\\\n   492\\\\\\\\t+---------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------+\\\\\\\\n   493\\\\\\\\t| Consumer host | Local parser implementation   | Alternative              |\\\\\\\\n   494\\\\\\\\t+===============+===============================+==========================+\\\\\\\\n   495\\\\\\\\t| JVM / CLJ     | Generated Java parser in an   | Configured parsing       |\\\\\\\\n   496\\\\\\\\t|               | isolated worker or worker     | service                  |\\\\\\\\n   497\\\\\\\\t|               | process                       |                          |\\\\\\\\n   498\\\\\\\\t+---------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------+\\\\\\\\n   499\\\\\\\\t| Node / CLJS   | Generated JavaScript parser   | Local sidecar or remote  |\\\\\\\\n   500\\\\\\\\t|               | in a worker; TypeScript       | service                  |\\\\\\\\n   501\\\\\\\\t|               | compiled at build             |                          |\\\\\\\\n   502\\\\\\\\t+---------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------+\\\\\\\\n   503\\\\\\\\t| Dart / CLJD   | Generated Dart parser (the    | Sidecar where supported, |\\\\\\\\n   504\\\\\\\\t|               | local implementation for      | or a remote service;     |\\\\\\\\n   505\\\\\\\\t|               | Python since 2026-10-17; a    | otherwise unsupported    |\\\\\\\\n   506\\\\\\\\t|               | grammar without a Dart helper | outcome                  |\\\\\\\\n   507\\\\\\\\t|               | answers `unavailable-parser`) |                          |\\\\\\\\n   508\\\\\\\\t+---------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------+\\\\\\\\n   509\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   510\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   511\\\\\\\\tA CLJD application can compile through a service without bundling ANTLR.\\\\\\\\n   512\\\\\\\\tIt can also consume previously compiled rows without any parser.\\\\\\\\n   513\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   514\\\\\\\\tFull offline local compilation on all three hosts requires validated\\\\\\\\n   515\\\\\\\\tparser artifacts for all three. Service-based portability must not be\\\\\\\\n   516\\\\\\\\tadvertised as offline portability.\\\\\\\\n  4380\\\\\\\\treporting is supplied by a listener, while recovery may insert/delete\\\\\\\\n  4381\\\\\\\\ttokens, continue, or raise recognition errors. The integration must\\\\\\\\n  4382\\\\\\\\tcontrol both mechanisms.\\\\\\\\n  4383\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  4384\\\\\\\\t### 10.1 Boundary policy\\\\\\\\n  4385\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  4386\\\\\\\\tFor lexer and parser:\\\\\\\\n  4387\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  4388\\\\\\\\t1. Remove default console listeners.\\\\\\\\n  4389\\\\\\\\t2. Install boundary transformations that classify diagnostics as plain\\\\\\\\n  4390\\\\\\\\t   data.\\\\\\\\n  4391\\\\\\\\t3. Select a pinned recovery strategy.\\\\\\\\n  4392\\\\\\\\t4. Catch recognized parsing failures at the host boundary.\\\\\\\\n  4393\\\\\\\\t5. Export recovery markers and terminal parse status.\\\\\\\\n  4394\\\\\\\\t6. Retain no exception, recognizer, token, or host stack object in\\\\\\\\n  4395\\\\\\\\t   payloads.\\\\\\\\n  4396\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  4397\\\\\\\\tA default strict profile refuses executable publication after any\\\\\\\\n  4398\\\\\\\\tlexical or syntax error, even when ANTLR constructed a recovered CST. An\\\\\\\\n  4399\\\\\\\\tIDE profile may publish partial syntax for tooling on a separate medium.\\\\\\\\n  4400\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  4401\\\\\\\\tWorker crashes, timeouts, resource exhaustion, grammar incompatibility,\\\\\\\\n  4402\\\\\\\\tand internal defects remain distinct from invalid source.\\\\\\\\n  4403\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  4404\\\\\\\\t### 10.2 Qualified outcome maps\\\\\\\\n  4405\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  4406\\\\\\\\tEvery stage reports through qualified outcome maps in the shape of\\\\\\\\n  4407\\\\\\\\tsection 6.2: a stream outcome wrapping a compiler outcome. The compiler\\\\\\\\n  4408\\\\\\\\toutcome names its phase and reason with qualified keywords:\\\\\\\\n  4409\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  4410\\\\\\\\t- Parse errors: `:yang.compile/syntax-error` from the parse phase.\\\\\\\\n  4411\\\\\\\\t- Semantic errors: unbound names, type errors, unsupported features,\\\\\\\\n  4412\\\\\\\\t  from the analyze phase.\\\\\\\\n  4413\\\\\\\\t- Lowering failures: unhandled CST constructs, grammar/profile mismatch,\\\\\\\\n  4414\\\\\\\\t  from the lower phase.\\\\\\\\n  4415\\\\\\\\t- Operational failures: worker crash, timeout, cancellation, resource\\\\\\\\n  4416\\\\\\\\t  limit, reported as operational events and never as language errors.\\\\\\\\n  4417\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  4418\\\\\\\\t### 10.3 Proposed diagnostic record\\\\\\\\n  4419\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  4420\\\\\\\\t```clojure\\\\\\\\n  4421\\\\\\\\t{:yang.diagnostic/code :yang.python/unbound-local\\\\\\\\n  4422\\\\\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/phase :yang.compile/analyze\\\\\\\\n  4423\\\\\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/severity :yang.diagnostic/error\\\\\\\\n  4424\\\\\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/request [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"client-token\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 12]\\\\\\\\n  4425\\\\\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/attempt [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"worker-token\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 4]\\\\\\\\n  4426\\\\\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/source [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"source-unit\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 3]\\\\\\\\n  4427\\\\\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/span {:start-byte 41 :end-byte 42}\\\\\\\\n  4428\\\\\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/arguments {:name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\n  4429\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_34\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg -n 'php/scope-of|php/this-of|php/has-this|php/this-or-null|called-class' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc | head -30; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '3317,3349p;52