{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-20 20:28:46 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-21 03:28:46 +07\n\nD10 is compatible with the architecture. An immutable composition can select Clojure semantics by default, keep native semantics available by revision, and give each task one Clojure exception domain. **R7 does not yet specify a working path through that design.** With both revisions installed, the normal frontend request is ambiguous. An explicit legacy pin encounters a second problem at admission because the proposed entry hook has a different arity from the frozen Python export.\n\n| Severity | Section | Evidence | Correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **High** | [§§2.1a, 6.5, P3′](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:479) | `yang.frontend/select` returns `:yang.frontend/ambiguous` when two revisions match. The REPL passes an ID-only request through unchanged. The landed Python entry is `[:yang/python \"f4\"]`. Installing a second revision cannot by itself flip the default. [Selector](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:193) · [REPL entry](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2353) · [Python manifest](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:70) | Put the preferred `[id revision]` in the composition’s immutable configuration and apply it at the normal request entry. Gate both revisions installed together, an ordinary request selecting Clojure semantics, an explicit legacy pin preserving native behavior, and an in-flight request retaining its original snapshot. |\n| **High** | [§§6.3–6.4, 7.3, P3′–P4′](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:422) | `:unit/run-main` always requires `[body-fn ambient-resolver]`, and admission requires exact lambda arity. Frozen `py/run-main` is `(fn [body] ...)`. JS also emits one operand. PHP emits two or four, with the request stream in slot two and optional response and diagnostic streams after it. The promised 1:1 native mapping fails on Python before the corpus can run. [Python export](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:3725) · [JS entry](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc:2362) · [PHP entry](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3938) | Give each frontend an entry-lowering contract that emits the landed native call shape and the Clojure profile’s resolver-bearing shape. Gate actual entry execution, including PHP request-derived values and stream output. |\n| **High** | [§§2.1a, 5.2, 6.4–6.5](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:483) | §2.1a names five provenance fields. §6.5 names four and uses the descriptor address as the lowering profile. Two lowerer revisions can consume the same descriptor. Also, `validate-descriptor` never receives the selected runtime profile, and a verified dependency pin does not install its module in a cold task. [Compilation derivation contract](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.antlr.md:1095) · [Linker contract](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1384) | Use one derivation record that identifies the frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor, runtime closure, input and output. Reconcile descriptor and runtime pins by module symbol before lowering. Assign dependency-first installation to linked composition. Gate conflicting pins and first execution on a cold task. The resolver’s derivation belongs in provenance. Its live cell belongs to the task. |\n| **High** | [§§2.2, 4.3, 7.2–7.5](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:196) | One task-owned `clj/rt-ctx` is a sound ownership boundary. The unwind rule is incomplete, however. `raise` delivers to the first non-`:finally` boundary, while an `:effect` frame holds a vector `[tag handler-fn outer-k]`. A guest throw crossing a numeric-policy frame therefore has no valid exception action. Also, `clojure.core.impl` performs `:coll/unsupported-key` and calls `check-limit`, while the specified policy installation is in `clj.py/run-main`, which does not exist at P2′. [Effect operations](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:211) · [Policy installation](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:547) | Specify how `raise`, `perform`, abort and resume traverse each frame kind, restore the context and run cleanup exactly once. Give plain `yang.clojure` a cold-error policy at P2′. Describe `clojure.core.impl` as owning zero cells while declaring its runtime effects. Gate a throw across an unrelated effect handler and an invalid key through native Clojure entry. |\n| **High** | [§§6.2–6.4, P3′](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:469) | The design promises export **role** validation. Its executable check establishes qualification, closure membership and arity. A binary `clj/prim-get` satisfies those checks for `:op/add`. On the host path, registration retains the primitive profile address while validation requires the full arity record. [Frontend contract](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:329) · [Host registration](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:249) | Supply address-bound export-role evidence through the frontend contract or admitted profile, including accessor roles and executable literal targets. Resolve host profiles by their recorded addresses. Gate a same-arity, wrong-role target. This keeps language knowledge in the frontend and gives generic admission enough evidence to decide. |\n| **High** | [§§5.1–5.2, 6.1, P0′–P3′](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:267) | The example Python recipe removes the trailing `require`, enables C1 finalization and adds `yrt.*` dependencies. §5.2 applies standardization to all base preludes. Landed `py` has a trailing `require 'yang.call`, no C1 finalizer there, and a single `yang.call` pin. PHP also lacks that finalizer. Bundled Python is linear and PHP/JS are balanced, but bundled Clojure’s continuation family uses a left fold. Recording only `:linear` or `:balanced` cannot establish the freeze. [Python emitter](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:4105) · [PHP emitter](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:6297) · [Clojure bundle](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:994) | Label the example as a Track B recipe. Record bundled shape, linked trailing forms, dependency pins, and C1 behavior independently. Gate frozen tree and manifest addresses and C1 side-table identity or absence for all three native runtimes. Keep fresh default-profile unit goldens distinct from frozen runtime artifacts. |\n| **High** | [§7.5, P1′–P3′](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:642) | P2′ requires a real `clj → clj.py → clj` unwind, but P3′ first publishes `clj.py`. The migration also excludes `invoke-value` while the replacement dispatcher accepts authenticated function cells only. The existing Clojure fixture requires a locally bound map invoked with `:k` to return `9`. Finally, `impl-*` prefixes protect linked definition names, but bundled bare `get` and `assoc` still resolve through the source store before VM primitives. [Collection-call fixture](/tmp/preludes-r7/test/yang/clojure_test.clj:3197) · [VM lookup](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:116) | Use Clojure-only consumers and synthetic nonzero depth/base fixtures at P1′. Gate native collection invocation and bundled primitive shadowing through the new standard library at P2′. Move the real cross-syntax unwind, including cleanup and context restoration, to P3′. |\n| **High** | [§§2.2, 4.1, 7.2, P0′](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:520) | The default path passes `integer/to-float` through guest `yrt.int/check-limit` before boxing it. Landed `integer/to-float` and `integer/true-div` produce host floating values or an overflow status. An integral JS `Number` can therefore enter a guest frame before its float kind is preserved. [Integer exports](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:414) · [Jing float carrier](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:242) | Expose boxed conversion and true-division results at the host boundary for the new profile. Keep the frozen native ABI. Gate an integral float and negative zero across capture and restore. Scope the zero-raw-double guarantee to profiles that use the boxed path. |\n| **Medium** | [§§8.1–8.2, 9–10](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:606) | §8.1 puts `defquoted` in `yang.core.prelude`, §8.2 and P0′ put it in `yang.core.defquoted`, and the revision history defers native consolidation to Track B. P1′ asks for a clean analyzer result before the three self-references disappear under the deferred schedule. Track B says the r6 gates apply *verbatim*, but the reviewed tree provides only a summary and no retrievable r6 gate table. §6.4 also still assigns native-oracle parity to the “default profiles.” | Use the dedicated macro namespace. Give native call-site migration one phase and make the graph gate reflect that choice. Attach the exact r6 P1/P4 gates or pin their immutable source. Apply native oracles to legacy pins and capability refusals to the default. Carry D3 and PHP’s `fpow-base` into Track B explicitly. |\n\n**Additional default-profile regressions.** Three small fixtures belong in the first Clojure-profile suite. An ordinary unqualified `:k` needs successful admission despite the “namespace non-empty” wording. Equal exact integers in different host carriers need the same map entry on insertion and lookup. A local or projected value equal to `:clj/unbound` must remain distinguishable from an absent binding. Also settle which traversal order the profile promises. §4.1’s type-rank order puts `nil` before integers, while Jing sorts by unsigned canonical encoded bytes, which put `0` before `nil`. [Key contract](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:170) · [Binding contract](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:534) · [Jing ordering](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:173)\n\n**Confirmed.**\n\n- The no-closed-registry boundary passes. Frontends own grammar-specific hooks and capability guards. Generic code can validate supplied contracts without dispatching on language names. The declared default refusals cover classes, generators including generator expressions, typed `except`, `with`, and kwargs. [Ownership](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:322) · [Capabilities](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:351)\n- The five-slot frame is grounded in landed Python and PHP. Both already distinguish structural frame count from saved call depth. A Clojure-first implementation can exercise those slots with a synthetic context and leave native generator and safepoint migration deferred. [Python frames](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:284) · [PHP frames](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:190)\n- The landed counts match at `dbfef054`. `yang.core.prelude-admission` has **3** publics, with the proposed two bringing it to **5**. Pure `yang.core.prelude` has **11**, `yang.antlr.export` has **6**, and `yang.io` has **5**. Batch 2 also contains the PHP eval-transport extraction. The admission split landed in **`c9dbc991`**. §5.2 cites the earlier `1604aabe`. The D/D′ distinction correctly separates guest linker names from host emitter namespaces. The recorded graph check identifies macro self-loops and no multi-node SCCs. [Admission](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/core/prelude_admission.cljc:12) · [Emission](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc:11) · [Export](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/antlr/export.cljc:19) · [I/O](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/io.cljc:23) · [Eval transport](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_transport.cljc:37) · [Graph record](/tmp/preludes-r7/orchestrator-logs/1794767085-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-compilers-dry-round.md:860)\n\nThis was a read-only review. I ran the JVM `yang.frontend-test` suite. All **3 tests and 29 assertions passed**, including the two-revision ambiguity and explicit-pin cases. Four-host and language-oracle results were outside this run. [Catalog tests](/tmp/preludes-r7/test/yang/frontend_test.cljc:29)\n\nARCHITECT VERDICT: CHANGES REQUIRED — specify the default selector and frozen entry ABI, close the effect and admission contracts, and make each migration gate executable in its assigned slice."}}
